dent-finance-berlin-394263","company_name":"Moss","title":"Working Student Finance (f/m/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>At Moss, we give finance professionals the power to automate their day-to-day and make forward-thinking decisions.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our culture is what makes that possible: we play to win, we obsess over quality, and we win as One Moss, and it works. Moss closed a €35 million Series C in August 2026, crossing a €1 billion valuation, and became one of Europe's fintech unicorns. Join us for what's next.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join our <strong>Tax &amp; Accounting Team</strong> as a <strong>Working Student, Finance</strong> (f/m/d) onsite in Berlin. We offer a one-year contract (with the opportunity to prolong it) from October 2025.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a team of skilled professionals, who have experience from top investment banks and Big4 consultancy firms, who are eager to share our financial expertise and mentor young professionals like you. This role will give you the opportunity to take on a variety of financial tasks and work closely with senior leadership. We will guide you and help you gain a deep understanding and hands-on experience with accounting, tax, as well as our product.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll be doing<br /></strong><em>No day is the same at Moss, but here’s an idea of what you could be doing day-to-day:</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🌐 Finance 101s - Beyond the Basics: </strong>Dive into the heart of finance as you support our team with monthly finance tasks, mastering month-end closing, financial reconciliations, analyses, and annual financial statements and audits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🚀 Power Play in Product Development: </strong>You collaborate closely with our tech department to further innovate, shape and refine our product. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>💡 Tax Wizardry: </strong>Join forces with our team to optimize the group-wide tax landscape. You'll be one of the driving forces behind preparing tax reports for external stakeholders.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About you</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We think you’ll need the following <strong>qualifications</strong> to succeed in this role: </em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Currently enrolled in a degree program such as Finance, Economics, or other related subjects and looking for a working student position for 20 hours a week</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in German (C1) and English (C1)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Previous internship experience or working experience, ideally within Finance </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>In addition, here are the <strong>skills and attributes</strong> we are looking for:</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💡 <strong>Keen Accuracy:</strong> You don't just focus on tasks; you make them flawless. Your meticulous attention to detail is beyond average.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌐 <strong>Ownership &amp; Drive:</strong> Take charge! Own your tasks, drive them to completion, and don't hesitate to seek help and guidance to deliver top-notch work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤝 <strong>Integrity First:</strong> Trustworthy, reliable, and unafraid to speak up when something's not right. That's the level of integrity we're looking for.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 <strong>Seek The Exceptional:</strong> Your appetite for learning knows no bounds. You're on a quest for excellence, and that hunger fuels everything you do.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Moss</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Moss is the Finance AI platform for Europe's mid-sized businesses, giving companies real-time visibility and full control over their spend. By automating card issuing, invoice management and expenses, Moss simplifies financial workflows and frees finance and accounting teams from manual, administrative work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Berlin and used by more than 10,000 businesses including Flink, Schufa, n8n and Auto1, Moss has raised €220+ million to date and operates in Germany, the Netherlands, the UK and further EU markets. In August 2026, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.getmoss.com/magazine/moss-series-c?origin-page=en-us%2Fcareers"><u>Moss closed a €35 million Series C </u></a>led by Portage, crossing a €1 billion valuation and becoming one of Europe's newest fintech unicorns. Moss is backed by investors including Valar Ventures, Tiger Global, Global Founders Capital, Cherry Ventures, A-Star.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a team of 300+ people from 50+ nationalities across 5 offices in Europe and we hire, reward, and grow people based on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/moss-finance/life/c2ac8184-5388-4962-ad07-e0bcbfe080f0/?viewAsMember=true"><u>Moss DNA</u></a>: playing to win, obsessing over quality, winning as One Moss. If that's how you want to work, we want to hear from you. - here's <strong>what else to expect:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Top-of-market compensation package, including equity. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our vibrant offices are at the heart of our culture, where in-person time fuels collaboration and connection over weekly breakfasts and Friday demos.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Additional benefits include: 20 days “work from abroad”, 600EUR/GBP Learning &amp; Development Budget, and other local benefits.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Unless stated otherwise, benefits apply to full-time positions (interns and working students receive a tailored package).</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>By applying for the above position, you will confirm that you have reviewed and agreed to our </strong></em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.getmoss.com/privacy-policy"><em><strong><u>Data Privacy Policy</u></strong></em></a><em><strong>.</strong></em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/moss/working-student-finance-berlin-394263","tags":["Enablement"],"job_types":["Intern"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1795848014},{"slug":"forward-deployed-engineer-berlin-424002","company_name":"Rematiq Gmbh","title":"Forward Deployed Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We are building the first AI-native platform for <strong>automated product compliance in MedTech</strong>. REMATIQ turn hundreds of page of complex regulations (like MDR and FDA guidance) into structured, actionable requirements that plug directly into our customers’ development and quality processes. The result: life‑saving medical devices reach patients faster and safer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the job</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Forward Deployed Engineer, you build software with and for our customers. Existing customers ask for more than the standard product does. They want further use cases, integrations with their own systems and workflows specific to their organisation. You sit with the customer's team, scope the problem and build the solution end to end. It runs at the customer as custom software or becomes a feature of the REMATIQ web app.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a software engineering role with customer contact, not a consulting role. You work closely with our AI Deployment Strategists, Product and the platform team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe in the value of in-person collaboration and work in a hybrid setup, with the team coming together in our office in the heart of Berlin-Mitte typically four days per week.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How you'll contribute</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scope with the customer:</strong> Sit with their project team and subject-matter experts, understand the workflow and its constraints, and cut the problem into something that can ship in weeks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build and ship end to end:</strong> Design, develop and deploy the solution, including backend services, integrations, AI workflows and the interface it needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run what you shipped:</strong> Operate it in production, fix what breaks, and be the customer's technical contact for it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build integrations:</strong> Connect REMATIQ to the systems customers already use in their development and quality processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Move custom work into the product:</strong> Build features in the web app and work with the platform team to turn one customer's solution into a product capability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Find the next use case:</strong> Spot further use cases while you work with the customer and scope them together with Delivery.</p></li></ul><h2>Our stack</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work in a modern TypeScript‑first monorepo:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Core:</strong> Node.js 20+, TypeScript 5+, pnpm workspaces, Turborepo.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Frontend:</strong> React (Vite), Tailwind CSS, and design system.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Backend &amp; workflows:</strong> Express-based services, with DBOS for durable workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data &amp; storage:</strong> PostgreSQL with pgvector, Prisma ORM, Azure Blob Storage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI &amp; observability:</strong> Azure OpenAI, Langfuse, Sentry, plus logging/tracing with tools like Winston and OpenTelemetry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Dev experience:</strong> AI‑assisted workflows with Cursor and Claude Code, integrated into our TypeScript‑first monorepo and review process.</p></li></ul><h2>What you'll bring</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a software engineer who ships production software and is equally at home in a customer's meeting room.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You may be a strong fit if you have:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Relevant background:</strong> 3+ years as a software engineer shipping production software, ideally including forward deployed, solutions engineering or other customer-facing engineering work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product management or team lead experience:</strong> Some experience as a product manager or team lead, where you owned scope, priorities and requirements for what is being built, is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong TypeScript and Node.js backend experience:</strong> You build and operate production services and can contribute to React frontends where needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Solid database fundamentals:</strong> PostgreSQL (ideally), including data modelling, migrations and performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Integration experience:</strong> You have connected a product to enterprise systems through APIs, SSO or data exchange, and have worked within a customer's IT and security constraints.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience building with LLMs:</strong> You have put LLM-driven features into production and know how to make them predictable and reviewable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong customer presence:</stron