d, tested and flown.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work closely with the other engineering disciplines, and you will report to the Principal Engineer of the project.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own work packages or full future projects</strong> in avionics, communications and power, from concept through verification, delivering on time, on quality and on cost.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Define functional breakdowns and high-level requirements</strong>, flow them down to avionics subsystems, and manage the associated technical baselines so the design meets the needs of each project.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Develop system architectures and conceptual designs</strong>, perform avionics-related technical trade-offs, and carry out budget and performance analyses (power, mass, data, thermal interfaces).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Write development, implementation, verification and validation plans</strong>, and drive them through to completion with the teams involved.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Develop hardware solutions</strong> for future projects, from requirements to integration and test support.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we would love to see from you</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role, ideally, you will have the following:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proven hands-on experience in designing electrical systems</strong> for spacecraft or other aerospace platforms, with a clear record of delivering them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A broad understanding of the full functional chain</strong> of space-based avionics, communications and power systems, and how the pieces interact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Able to work effectively with neighboring subsystems </strong>(thermal, GNC, propulsion, flight software, operations), understanding their interfaces and constraints well enough to resolve cross-disciplinary trade-offs and keep interface control documents aligned.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong systems engineering skills</strong>: defining requirements and their flow-down, managing technical baselines, and producing architectures and trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience with budgets and performance analysis</strong> (power, mass, data, thermal) to support design decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on experience with development, assembly, integration and testing</strong> of electrical units for space applications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong written and oral communication skills in English</strong>, with the ability to explain technical issues clearly to engineers, managers and partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A degree in Electrical Engineering, Telecommunications, Aerospace Engineering or a related field</strong>, or equivalent practical experience in the relevant domain.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a guideline, candidates typically bring 5+ years of relevant experience in aerospace system design. We value demonstrated capability over the number of years, so we welcome applications from candidates with a strong track record who may have followed a non-linear path.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Skills and Behaviours</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Analytical and problem-solving mindset</strong>, with the ability to structure complex problems and reach sound decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Organised and pragmatic</strong>, able to set priorities across several work packages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Positive and flexible</strong>, with a can-do attitude to get the job done.