-level performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and maintain sensor requirements, specifications, and interfaces in alignment with overall spacecraft mission and system requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assess sensor technologies, evaluate design trade-offs, and drive technical decisions to ensure optimal performance, reliability, and suitability for the mission.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure proper integration of navigation sensors into the spacecraft avionics architecture.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Supplier and Component Management</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the technical focal point for navigation sensor suppliers throughout the component development lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate technical reviews, manage supplier deliverables, and resolve technical issues throughout development and procurement.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Testing, Verification and Certification</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and maintain verification and qualification strategies for navigation sensor components and systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and review test plans, procedures, and acceptance criteria.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate and support component-level testing, environmental qualification, functional verification, and system integration testing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analyze test results, assess compliance with requirements, and drive resolution of identified anomalies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare and maintain verification evidence and technical documentation to support qualification, certification, and mission readiness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support reviews and technical interactions with cu