:1.5em">Experience working in multidisciplinary engineering environments and coordinating technical activities across teams.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good level of understanding of the following domains:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Navigation, Guidance and Control</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Navigation sensors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hardware testing</p></li></ul></li></ul><h3>Preferred Qualifications</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency with simulation and software development tools (e.g. Python, Github, C/C++).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with spacecraft navigation sensors such as GNSS receivers, inertial measurement units (IMUs), accelerometers, gyroscopes, magnetometers, star trackers, or optical navigation sensors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with spacecraft or aircraft platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with GNC architectures, navigation algorithms, sensor fusion, and estimation techniques.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why you should join us!</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What makes us special here at The Exploration Company and why we think you will enjoy working here is:  </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re Agile - we make decisions fast whilst keeping our goals and systems in mind </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re Open and Collaborative - we are transparent about risks and obstacles, so that we can cooperate to overcome them  </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have a lot of Fun - we refuel our energy knowing we are democratising space. It’s a wonderful and rare opportunity, are YOU up for the challenge?  </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We'd love to hear from you if you wish to be a part of our journey. Please submit your CV now for immedia