height:1.5em">The successful candidate will act as a senior technical contributor across the ECLSS perimeter, supporting CFD analyses, complex technical topics, challenging designs and models, and driving cross-functional activities with internal teams, suppliers and agencies. A particular focus will be placed on strengthening our capabilities in CFD, while bringing hands-on experience from the development and qualification of Environmental Control, Air Revitalization, Air Circulation or HVAC systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work closely with the ECLSS team and will report directly to the ECLSS Principal Engineer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Key responsibilities</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead and support CFD activities for cargo bay and vestibule, including modelling strategy, assumptions, boundary conditions, model justification.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the development of ECLSS system (Air circulation, pressurization control, crew emergency), identifying critical design aspects and potential technical issues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide technical support during product development, from requirements and architecture through detailed design, verification and qualification logic.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support definition of the environmental test campaigns (objectives, test bench, planning, test article procurement)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define CFD validation and verification strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Correlate analytical, Ecosim and CFD models for the air revitilization and pressure control system with test data and define appropriate acceptance criteria and uncertainty margins.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead focused technical working groups, trade-offs and root-cause investigations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive co-engineering activities with suppliers, other spacecraft disciplines and external agencies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the preparation of system, sub-system and component reviews</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the continuous improvement of ECLSS engineering methods, modelling practices and development processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Foster a culture of technical excellence, accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Profile</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8+ years of relevant experience in Environment Control System design for cabin, preferably within aircraft, space or military industries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong expertise in CFD, including model construction, turbulence modelling, meshing, convergence, validation and correlation against test data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in ANSYS Fluent, STAR-CCM+, or OpenFOAM<strong>.</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with GitHub and Python for analysis automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of low-pressure and low-speed air-flow systems, including pressure losses, fans/blowers, ducting, valves and system-level performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in hardware/product development and testing, ideally from early design through qualification.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with environmental testing such as TVAC, thermal balance, mechanical tests, pressure tests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with relevant NASA standards and verification practices is highly desirable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to lead technical discussions and communicate effectively with suppliers, agencies and multidisciplinary engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pragmatic, ha