sses.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Be Doing</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead Enterprise technical discovery, deep-dive calls, and tailored demos, showing how n8n fits into complex customer environments while addressing security, scalability, and reliability requirements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with Account Executives to assess technical fit, shape deal strategy, and handle technical objections, delivering demos grounded in real Enterprise workflows and use cases</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own Enterprise POCs end-to-end, from scoping success criteria to hands-on technical guidance throughout the evaluation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help customers validate n8n in real-world conditions and capture POC learnings to improve qualification, conversion, and handoff to Solution Architecture/Customer Success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build strong relationships with IT, Security, Platform, and Engineering stakeholders, acting as the primary technical contact during Enterprise evaluations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clearly explain n8n’s approach to security, deployment, governance, and scale, helping customers plan adoption beyond their first use case</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with Sales to improve Enterprise technical discovery, demos, and POC frameworks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide structured feedback from Enterprise customers to Product and Engineering, and contribute to enablement materials that strengthen Enterprise sales motions</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Must-have</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>💼 Sales Engineering Experience: </strong>You have 6+ years of experience in a technical pre-sales or Sales Engineering role, ideally within B2B SaaS, with direct exposure to enterprise customers</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><str