s, and drive high-performance within their teams.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Driving the Implementation of People Programs</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the people development function to drive the implementation and adoption of people programs within your designated area.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support leaders and teams through change and take ownership of core programs, e.g performance feedback, ensuring effective delivery and desired outcomes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Navigating Employee Relations with Empathy and Expertise</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the resolution of employee relations matters, including conflict resolution, disciplinary actions, and sensitive workplace dynamics (either directly or in close collaboration with our Employee Relations Specialist).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure situations are handled thoughtfully, consistently, and in line with our values and legal requirements.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Creating a Seamless Employee Experience through Cross-Functional Partnership</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with cross-functional People &amp; Culture teams to ensure a seamless employee experience and embed cohesive ways of working between the business and our department.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong><br /></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Multiple years of experience as a People Partner </strong>in a complex global company, ideally in a fast-paced, scaling context, with deep experience in partnering with leaders across different countries, including the US.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong business acumen and strategic thinking </strong>to understand how different business areas operate, connect people priorities with business needs, and confidently act as a trusted advisor to leaders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong collaboration and cross-functional partnership skills</strong>, working effectively as a team player with stakeholders at multiple levels across the organization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clear, confident, and empathetic communication, stakeholder management, and influencing skills</strong>, with the ability to adapt to different audiences, build trusted relationships, and create alignment on complex or sensitive topics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Action-oriented ownership </strong>to proactively drive topics forward, navigate obstacles, and ensure initiatives are successfully implemented to achieve desired outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Skilled at systemic thinking and problem-solving,</strong> understanding how people, processes, and structures interconnect to identify underlying patterns and develop thoughtful, sustainable solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Global mindset and flexibility</strong> to thrive in an international setup, including early-evening meetings when needed to collaborate with US-based colleagues as well as occasional business trips to Düsseldorf</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full professional fluency in <strong>English and German</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ideally, experience working with <strong>works councils </strong>and navigating the associated processes and requirements.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Join Us?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Global teamwork:</strong> We work together across departmental and national borders on our vision of bringing the Toniebox to every child's room in the world.</p></li><li><p style=