ements and record results accurately, maintaining clear and traceable laboratory records.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support investigations into unexpected results, process variation, material issues, and non-conformances.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain laboratory organisation, stock levels, equipment readiness, waste handling, and safety standards.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What we are looking for</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in a laboratory, chemical-processing, manufacturing, or other practical technical environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A technical qualification or practical training in chemistry, chemical engineering, materials science, laboratory science, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A careful and methodical approach to weighing, measurement, sample handling, documentation, and process control.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical understanding of laboratory safety, chemical handling, personal protective equipment, and safe working procedures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong attention to detail and the ability to follow written procedures consistently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative, reliable, and proactive approach to working with engineers, scientists, technicians, and production teams.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Desirable experience</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid rocket propellants, energetic materials, polymers, binders, oxidisers, metallic fuels, or catalysts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Laboratory-scale mixing, casting, curing, grinding, sample preparation, or chemical processing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Propellant characterisation, burn-rate measurement, thermal analysis, rheology, mechanical testing, or compatibility testing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with labo