ny_name":"Orbem","title":"Occupational Health & Safety Expert , Fachkraft für Arbeitssicherheit (f/m/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We see the potential inside everything and everyone. Starting with you.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Orbem uses AI to industrialize MRI, delivering non-invasive insight into everything from fruits to eggs to the human body. We are transforming what is becoming the world's largest biological dataset into actionable intelligence to reduce waste, increase quality, and accelerate the shift toward a more sustainable and healthier future.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Headquartered and founded in Munich, Germany, with an office now in Houston, Texas, our world-class team is scaling inside-out technology to transform how humanity sees and understands biological matter.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Help us see what's possible. Join us.</strong></p><h1><strong>Your Role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Orbem’s appointed Fachkraft für Arbeitssicherheit, you are responsible for occupational health and safety at all Orbem sites and client installations, from laboratories and MRI environments to the workshop. You are the subject-matter expert Orbem relies on for the hard safety calls: you set the standards, build the systems behind them and lead the safety projects that matter most. You work with a high degree of autonomy. Your impact comes from technical depth, influence and mentoring. You decide independently on risk assessment methods, technical standards and corrective actions, align with management on measures with high cost or cross-team impact, and escalate imminent dangers and legal non-compliance early.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Your Day-to-Day</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Legal Occupational Safety:</strong> You perform all duties of a designated occupational safety specialist under § 7 ASiG and ensure compliance with the relevant regulations (ArbSchG, GefStoffV, BioStoffV, StrlSchG, ArbStättV).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Safety Strategy &amp; Systems:</strong> You own Orbem’s cross-functional OHS: risk assessments, incident management and compliance frameworks, including a legal register, standards, templates and escalation paths.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Subject-Matter Expertise:</strong> You are the key expert for safety in laboratory and MRI environments (magnetic fields, hazardous and biological substances) and set the standard for quality in this area.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Projects:</strong> You lead complex, cross-functional safety projects, such as new labs and build-outs, and coordinate contractor safety.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Incidents &amp; Root Cause Analysis:</strong> You investigate incidents and near-misses, run root cause analyses and follow every corrective action through to closure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Training &amp; Mentoring: </strong>You build the training and instruction programme, document knowledge, give internal talks and mentor colleagues and the safety contacts in the teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ESG: </strong>Support the team with knowledge, advice and guidance on environmental and sustainability topics, and help develop how ESG fits into Orbem as the topic grows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Authorities &amp; Audits:</strong> You are the contact for authorities, auditors and external partners on specialist matters.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your responsibilities include:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keeping Orbem compliant with German occupational health and safety law, from risk assessments and training to incident follow-up and contact with authorities. You will also be focusing on the development of the OHS function at Orbem.</p><p style="mi