://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/my-humancapital-gmbh/safety-engineer-luft-und-raumfahrt-bonn-457008","tags":["Quality Management"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag","berufserfahren"],"location":"Bonn","created_at":1795802447},{"slug":"growth-engineer-london-414989","company_name":"Lovable","title":"Growth Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> <br />We’re looking for a full-stack engineer obsessed with Lovable’s growth engine - turning first touches into daily habits, and daily habits into a thriving ecosystem and real revenue. One sprint you’re shipping onboarding and activation flows; the next you’re crafting distribution rails and monetization features that help builders reach more users and keep them around. You think in React and APIs, but your first instinct is always: does this make users more successful, more often?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Coding skills + excellent taste + growth instincts + product obsession = you.</strong><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Lovable?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lovable is the software creation platform that gives people the power to act on the problems closest to them. For decades, turning an idea into software required so much capital, technical fluency, and time that many ideas never came to life. Lovable is the counterargument: a platform for all people with ideas, ambition, and problems worth solving. From solopreneurs to small business owners to teams at companies like Adidas and Zendesk, people have built over 60 million projects on Lovable since its launch in November 2024. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building a generational company from Stockholm, with growing teams in London, Boston, New York, and San Francisco. Our team is small, talent-dense, and moving quickly, with a culture rooted in extreme ownership, high velocity, and low-ego collaboration. We look for people who care deeply, ship fast, and are eager to make a dent in the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lovable is one of TIME’s 100 Most Influential Companies and has been recognized on the Forbes AI 50 and CNBC Disruptor 50, reflecting our momentum as one of Europe’s fastest-growing AI companies and one of the most ambitious places to build in this next era of software.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience building and growing user-facing products in high-performing teams, ideally including growth work, marketplaces/platforms, or communities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong product sense and UX taste for multi-sided systems with creators, learners, and customers - you can see problems from multiple sides and design for all of them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable using data, funnels, analytics, attribution, and A/B testing to shape what you build and how you iterate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Skilled at designing, measuring, and iterating experiments, and thorough in setting up growth systems “right” from the start.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience collaborating across functions (design, marketing, partnerships, support, data) to launch and grow new product surfaces and ecosystems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enjoys designing reusable growth, ecosystem, and monetization tools that other builders can plug into, with a pragmatic and detail-oriented mindset.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Motivated by helping others succeed and by seeing impact through engagement, measurable results, and revenue - you care about the scoreboard as much as the code.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In one sentence: You will build the growth, ecosystem, and monetization systems that make Lovable - and the apps built on it - sticky, discoverable, and revenue-generating.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ship and iterate activation, monetization and retention experiences that create fast, repeatable value and turn first-time users into long-term fans.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build distribution rails for user apps: SEO and performance, shareable moments, social previews, email and lifecycle journeys, and other growth hooks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ship marketplace and ecosystem features for publishing, discovering, and reusing apps, templates, components, and services - plus profiles, reviews, and matching between builders and customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and implement monetization and pricing flows: payments, subscriptions, access control, plans, paywalls, billing integration, and revenue-share models that work for creators, customers, and Lovable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the analytics and experimentation foundations - events, funnels, attribution, and A/B tests - so the team can understand what works and double down on it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate closely with design, marketing, partnerships, and support to launch and grow new surfaces across the product and ecosystem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the experience relentlessly Lovable while making growth the engine, not the afterthought.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our tech stack</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building with tools that both humans and AI love:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Frontend: React</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backend: Golang and Rust</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cloud: Cloudflare, GCP, AWS, many LLM providers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">DevOps and tooling: GitHub Actions, Grafana, OTEL, infra-as-code (Terraform)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About your application</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please submit your application in English. It’s our company language, so you’ll be speaking lots of it if you join.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We treat all candidates equally - if you’re interested, please apply through our careers portal.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/lovable/growth-engineer-london-414989","tags":["EPD"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795848015},{"slug":"performance-marketer-paid-social-london-472630","company_name":"Lovable","title":"Performance Marketer, Paid Social","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>TL;DR -</strong> We're looking for a hands-on paid social marketer to run Meta as our core channel and test other social platforms. You'll build agents with Lovable that read performance, move budgets, catch issues, and make changes. This is an IC role for someone senior who likes being in the detail and building the machine, not just operating it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why Lovable?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lovable is the software creation platform that gives people the power to act on the problems closest to them. For decades, turning an idea into software required so much capital, technical fluency, and time that many ideas never came to life. Lovable is the counterargument: a platform for all people with ideas, ambition, and problems worth solving. From solopreneurs to small business owners to teams at companies like Adidas and Zendesk, people have built over 60 million projects on Lovable since its launch in November 2024. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building a generational company from Stockholm, with growing teams in London, Boston, New York, and San Francisco. Our team is small, talent-dense, and moving quickly, with a culture rooted in extreme ownership, high velocity, and low-ego collaboration. We look for people who care deeply, ship fast, and are eager to make a dent in the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lovable is one of TIME’s 100 Most Influential Companies and has been recognized on the Forbes AI 50 and CNBC Disruptor 50, reflecting our momentum as one of Europe’s fastest-growing AI companies and one of the most ambitious places to build in this next era of software.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>7+ years running paid social</strong>. You've owned significant budgets on Meta, and you've run or tested at least one other social channel, such as TikTok, Snap, Reddit.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Automation-led</strong>. You don't do by hand what a script or an agent could do. You've built automations for reporting, budget pacing, or optimisation, and you're comfortable with platform APIs and pulling your own data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Creative-obsessed</strong>. On social, the creative does most of the targeting. You know what makes a thumb stop, you can brief and iterate with the creative team, and you keep a high-volume, diversified pipeline moving: UGC, creator content, static, video. You've taken a paid social channel from small to large and kept it efficient on the way up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Efficiency-minded</strong>. You think in CAC and payback, and you can tell efficient growth from spend that just looks like growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A disciplined tester</strong>. You know how to stand up a new channel properly: clean test design, enough budget to read a result, and the judgement to call it quickly either way.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on by choice</strong>. You'd rather be driving impact than in a deck. You like the detail, and you build things yourself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Already building with AI.</strong> You use AI day to day, you're comfortable building agents, and you'll use Lovable to ship the tools this role runs on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical spike</strong>. You go deep in at least one of: data analytics, data engineering, or tracking and measurement. You don't need all three at that level, but you need to be strong in one, comfortable in the rest, and delivering the work yourself.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run paid social end to end. Own Meta as a core channel. You set the account structure, the audiences, the bids, the budgets, and the targets, and you know when to lean on Advantage+ and when to take back control.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Open new channels. Test TikTok, Snap, Reddit and other social platforms with a clear hypothesis and a clear kill or scale call. Grow the ones that earn it, and hold them to the same efficiency bar as Meta.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Automate the day-to-day. Build agents and automations with Lovable that read performance, pace and shift budgets, flag issues like creative fatigue before they cost us, and make the changes. The goal is a paid program that mostly runs itself, with you steering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scale through creative. Keep a steady supply of fresh, diversified assets in market, work with the creative team and creative strategist, and know which concepts to push, iterate, or retire. Volume and variety are what keep social working.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Protect the signal. This is where your technical depth shows up, and you deliver it yourself rather than handing it to a data team. Build and debug the tracking (Meta CAPI, TikTok Events API, pixels, consent, and deduplication), and write the queries that judge channels on incrementality, using lift tests and holdouts, not just platform-reported ROAS.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay in the details. You'll be in the accounts, running tests on audiences, placements, and creative, and building most of this yourself. This is a role for someone who wants their hands on the work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/lovable/performance-marketer-paid-social-london-472630","tags":["GTM"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795848015},{"slug":"content-production-manager-united-kingdom-411847","company_name":"Progress Partners","title":"Content Production Manager","description":"<h1><strong>About Progress Partners</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Progress Partners is a fast-growing technology company building and scaling next-generation SaaS and mobile platforms. We blend creativity with data-driven execution to ship high-impact products, including AI-powered tools, productivity platforms, and workflow software, used by millions of people in more than 160 countries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our global team of experts in software development, product design, growth, and analytics collaborates across time zones to deliver category-defining innovations. We work end-to-end across the product lifecycle: design, build, launch, and scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re passionate about building transformative products, Progress Partners is a place to make a lasting impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>About the Role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hi, I’m <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/oleksandra-khilienko-843299226/">Oleksandra</a>, Head of Localization and Content at Progress Partners, and I’m hiring a Content Production Manager to join my team. We build consumer products ranging from utility tools to wellbeing and learning experiences, and many of them rely on rich in-app content, such as lessons, quizzes, stories, videos, and other formats, produced through a mix of AI workflows, in-house content specialists, and a network of freelancers. We’re now scaling that output across several products at once, and we need someone to own the engine full-time. You’ll run content production end to end, combining editorial judgment with strong project management to deliver high volumes of quality content on tight timelines. You’ll coordinate the work of our in-house content specialists and directly manage our freelance network, without direct reports initially.<br /><br />Progress Partners builds consumer web and mobile products used around the world, from utility tools to wellbeing and learning experiences, in up to 36 languages. The Content &amp; Localization team aims to own every word users read across our products and funnels, in every market.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are building this team from the ground up. You'll join early, shape how we work, and see your impact directly in product and revenue metrics.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-first.</strong> We use AI to produce and localize content at scale, and humans to set the standards, judge quality and decide.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Craftsmanship.</strong> We hire true subject-matter experts who take pride in their craft and bring the depth and judgment AI can't replace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fast and pragmatic.</strong> We launch quickly, balance quality with speed through a risk-based approach, and improve as we learn.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Async and remote.</strong> We work across time zones and write things down.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data-informed.</strong> We tie content and localization decisions to measurable outcomes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role reports to the Head of Localization &amp; Content.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and manage content production across products, from brief to publication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate AI-assisted content pipelines, including generation, review and import into our CMS.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Brief, manage and review freelancers: writers, video producers, editors, instructional designers and subject-matter experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run video production, including AI-generated video and captions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and track production timelines and capacity, and keep production within budget.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make sure content goes through quality review, originality checks and localization on time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor content performance and engagement, and feed insights into what we produce next.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep production systems topic-agnostic and reusable, so we can launch new verticals quickly.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">4–6 years in content production or editorial management for digital products, ideally in-app or educational content for learning or consumer apps</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing freelancers and remote experts at scale</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on content creation skills: you can write, edit and produce content yourself, not only coordinate it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong editorial skills and a high bar for content quality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with AI content and video tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent organization, with experience running several projects at once</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with metrics and content performance analysis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong written communication and the ability to work autonomously in a remote, async environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with ownership, transparency, and a results-driven mindset.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience producing bite-sized learning content, such as courses, lessons or quizzes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Instructional design experience, such as structuring lessons, learning paths or assessments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with CMS-based content workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience producing content for multiple languages.</p></li></ul><h1><strong> </strong></h1><h1><strong>In Your First 90 Days</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take over content production for an upcoming product launch and deliver it on schedule</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve our production workflow and tracking, and roll them out across products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a reliable pool of freelancers for video and other formats</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define content quality and originality checks for production</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>How We Work</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re fully remote and distributed across time zones. We default to async, communicate in writing, and trust people to deliver outcomes, not log hours. Decisions are transparent, ownership is clear, and your work is visible from day one.</p><h1><br /><strong>Interview Process</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've designed our interview process to be transparent, respectful of your time, and a genuine two-way conversation; we want to get to know you, and we want you to get to know us. You'll always know what stage you're at, what to expect next, and roughly how long things will take.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Initial screen with our Talent Acquisition Team - 30 min</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take-home assessment - 3 days</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final panel with Head of Localization and Content -  60 min</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What We Offer</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe great work starts with taking care of our people, and we want everyone on our team to have the support and resources they need to thrive, both professionally and personally. Here's what you can expect when you join our team:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remote-first:</strong> live and work wherever you're happiest and most productive.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible hours:</strong> we measure outcomes, not time spent at a desk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unlimited PTO:</strong> take the time you need to rest, recharge, and do your best work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; development budget:</strong> courses, books, conferences, certifications, whatever helps you grow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Home office &amp; wellness allowance:</strong> a dedicated budget to set up your workspace and support your health.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meet-up budget:</strong> funds to get together with teammates in person and spend time face to face.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A small, senior, collaborative team where your work is visible and your decisions matter.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The chance to build products used by millions of people across 160+ countries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Equal Opportunity</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Progress Partners is an equal opportunity employer, and we’re serious about building a diverse, inclusive team. We welcome applications from people of all genders, gender identities and expressions, sexual orientations, ages, ethnicities, nationalities, religions, disabilities, neurotypes, family situations, socioeconomic backgrounds, and life experiences.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire on skills, experience, potential, and values fit, never on protected characteristics. If you need accommodations during the application or interview process, just let us know.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/progress-partners/content-production-manager-united-kingdom-411847","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1795848015},{"slug":"implementation-specialist-london-80427","company_name":"Hawk","title":"Implementation Specialist","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hawk is the leading provider of AI-supported anti-money laundering and fraud detection technology. Banks and payment providers globally are using Hawk’s powerful combination of traditional rules and explainable AI to improve the effectiveness of their AML compliance and fraud prevention by identifying more crime while maximizing efficiency by reducing false positives. With our solution, we are playing a vital role in the global fight against Money Laundering, Fraud, or the financing of terrorism. We offer a culture of mutual trust, support and passion – while providing individuals with opportunities to grow professionally and make a difference in the world. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Your Mission</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an Implementation Specialist at Hawk, your responsibility is to transform customer requirements into a functioning solution that helps them achieve their business objectives around transaction monitoring, customer screening and fraud detection, alongside cutting-edge AI technologies. You start with a signed contract and support the customer until go-live. This includes translating policies, regulatory obligations and risk factors into Hawk's setup, data mapping, workflow configuration, UAT support and ensuring that key project timelines and milestones are met. You support our customers in realising true value by detecting more financial crime, allowing investigators to focus on what matters instead of drowning in false positives, and adopting state-of-the-art AI technologies.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Requirements and needs assessment: gather and analyse the customer's AML, fraud and screening requirements and advise on best-practice configuration.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Configuration: translate policies, screening algorithms, regulatory requirements and risk factors into Hawk's setup, covering rules, screening, customer risk rating and workflows.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Data mapping and integration: lead the technical deployment and integration with the customer's systems, via API or batch mechanisms.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Testing and go-live: support the customer through testing, UAT and sign-off, troubleshoot issues, and support a successful transition to a production environment.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Training and enablement: deliver training to the customer's teams from a functional as well as technical standpoint.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Project management: plan and run the implementation from signature to go-live on time and within scope, with documentation and regular stakeholder updates, combining hands-on work with project leadership.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Primary contact: be the first point of contact for implementation questions and issues.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaboration and feedback: work closely with Customer Value Partners for a smooth implementation, and bring actionable customer feedback and gaps to Product, Development and Hawk's GTM organisation.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Document every configuration decision and the reasoning behind it, so the setup holds up when the customer's auditor or regulator asks why a rule was set the way it was.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage each implementation task and the implementation success as an outcome you own, as directed by our Customer Value Partner, resulting in activity completion and a go-live on the dates you committed to.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Your Profile</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">6+ years in implementation consulting or solution consulting, with at least 3 of those years hands-on implementing AML, fraud or screening solutions.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Subject matter expertise in AML and compliance. You are familiar with key typologies and patterns, the regulatory expectations behind them, and how monitoring programmes as well as AI get examined.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can confidently stand in front of an MLRO and discuss and defend a rule set. This is a must-have, not a nice-to-have.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on data skills: SQL, APIs, CSV and JSON, and data modelling. You're familiar with standardised payment message formats, including SWIFT MT and ISO 20022, SEPA and card data.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integration literacy. You don't write production code, but you're at home with APIs, JSON payloads, SFTP configurations as well as SSO.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of taking complex implementations to go-live on time, ideally several in parallel, with banking customers or other financial institutions.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stakeholder alignment. You ensure that internal and external parties both have the information they need, keep them aligned and manage expectations.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to explain complexity simply. Imagine data models for compliance leads, fraud typologies for data engineers. You do it clearly in writing and in the room, in fluent English.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A degree in computer science, information systems, engineering, finance or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Bonus</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Business-fluent German, for working with our DACH customers.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CAMS (or equivalent) certification, or time spent in a second-line compliance or MLRO team.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style=