e a real difference.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The Job</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every patient room we deploy into puts another device on infrastructure we don't control, in a building we can't easily visit, running software that has to keep working. We're looking for an Engineer to own that problem: the systems, tooling, and infrastructure that let us ship to thousands of edge devices confidently and understand what they're doing once they're out there.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role, you will focus on the following areas of interest:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fleet Management:</strong> Build and run the systems that provision, monitor, and manage our devices in the field, from first boot in a hospital room to end of life.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>OTA &amp; Release Engineering:</strong> Own how software gets onto devices: staged rollouts, health checks, automatic rollback, and the confidence that a bad release won't take down a ward.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Observability:</strong> Design the telemetry, logging, and alerting that tell us a device is degrading before a nurse notices. Make remote debugging possible so we don't fly to fix things.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Device Bring-Up &amp; Debugging:</strong> Work with our hardware and firmware teams on new hardware revisions, reproduce field issues on the bench, and get to the bottom of problems that span kernel, driver, network, and application.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Infrastructure &amp; Tooling:</strong> Build the CI/CD, image builds, and internal tools that let the whole engineering team ship to hardware quickly and safely.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Documentation:</strong> Maintain clear and detailed documentation of your work to ensure easy collaboration and knowledge sharing within the team.</p><p style="min-height:1.