t and Project Management teams to provide robust risk insight and help ensure that project decisions are informed by a clear understanding of uncertainty and exposure.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a <strong>project risk-focused role</strong>, rather than an enterprise or corporate risk position. The successful candidate will have strong experience of <strong>quantitative risk analysis, QSRA, cost and schedule risk analysis and project risk modelling</strong>, ideally gained within major construction, infrastructure, engineering or other complex capital programmes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About us</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">CMR is first and foremost a team of people, passionate about the construction industry and changing the way project controls is provided.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a progressive and dynamic consultancy offering tailored project controls services across a range of industries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Purpose (Why we exist):</strong> Inspiring new ways to help shape our construction industry.<br /><strong>Our Ambition (What we want to achieve):</strong> Re-imagine project controls through a digital lens, being the obvious choice for clients and the place to grow together with intention.</p><h2>🔹 What’s in it for you?</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At CMR you will have the opportunity to professionally develop like nowhere you have worked before.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you demonstrate the capability, our merit-based system will enable you to develop quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use our in-house capability matrix to transparently track your progression and highlight development areas.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join our small, dynamic team where every member has the chance to make a significant impact, shaping the future direction of our company and making a real difference.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe in rewarding our team for their achievements, celebrating our successes but equally helping each other when things are tough.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity to work on a <strong>major, nationally significant infrastructure programme</strong>, gaining exposure to some of the most complex project risk challenges in the UK.</p></li></ul><h2>🔹 You’ll</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead and support the implementation of <strong>project risk management processes</strong> across complex infrastructure and construction projects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and maintain project risk registers, ensuring risks are clearly defined in terms of <strong>causes, events, impacts, probability, consequence and mitigation actions</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Facilitate risk identification and review workshops with Project Management, Planning, Commercial, Engineering and other project stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Challenge project teams to ensure risks are appropriately identified, assessed, quantified and actively managed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Undertake and support <strong>Quantitative Schedule Risk Analysis (QSRA)</strong> and <strong>Quantitative Cost Risk Analysis (QCRA)</strong> to assess the potential impact of uncertainty on project outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and maintain <strong>risk models</strong>, incorporating cost and schedule uncertainty, risk events, correlations and appropriate probability distributions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the development and review of <strong>risk allowances, contingency and management reserves</strong>, ensuring these are supported by robust quantitative analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analyse project cost and schedule exposure and provide insight into <strong>P-values, confidence levels, ranges and potential outcomes</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integrate risk information with project cost and schedule data to provide a consolidated view of project exposure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with Planning and Project Controls teams to understand the relationship between <strong>risk, uncertainty, programme and critical path</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor the effectiveness of mitigation strategies and assess changes in risk exposure over the project lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce clear and concise <strong>risk reporting, dashboards and management information</strong>, highlighting key exposures, trends, emerging risks and areas requiring management intervention.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide risk input into project forecasts, baseline reviews, change management and key project decision-making processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify and analyse <strong>emerging risks and opportunities</strong>, ensuring these are captured and appropriately assessed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the development of risk scenarios and sensitivity analysis to help project teams understand the potential impact of key uncertainties.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain appropriate risk governance, ensuring risk data is accurate, auditable and aligned with project controls requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work collaboratively with Project Managers, Project Controls Leads, Planners, Commercial Managers, Cost Managers and senior client stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Promote a proactive <strong>risk and uncertainty management culture</strong>, ensuring risk is used as a decision-making tool rather than simply a reporting requirement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to the continuous improvement of CMR's project risk methodologies, processes, tools and ways of working.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support Senior Risk Managers and Project Controls Leads in delivering high-quality risk management services to our clients.</p></li></ul><h2>🔹 We’re looking for:</h2><h3><strong>Essential</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in a <strong>project risk management</strong> role within major construction, infrastructure, engineering or another complex capital project environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of <strong>project risk management methodologies and quantitative risk analysis</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience undertaking or supporting <strong>Quantitative Schedule Risk Analysis (QSRA)</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience undertaking or supporting <strong>Quantitative Cost Risk Analysis (QCRA)</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience developing, maintaining and interrogating <strong>project risk registers and risk models</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of the relationship between <strong>risk, cost, schedule, contingency and project forecasting</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience facilitating risk workshops with project and technical stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience assessing probability, impact, uncertainty and risk exposure and translating this into meaningful project insight.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical and numerical skills, with the ability to interpret complex project data and identify trends and areas of concern.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good understanding of project controls and how risk interacts with <strong>planning, cost, commercial and change management</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong stakeholder management skills, with the confidence to challenge assumptions and constructively influence project teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills, with the ability to explain complex quantitative analysis clearly to both technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proactive approach to identifying emerging risks and opportunities and improving project performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in a complex, multi-stakeholder project environment.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Desirable</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working on <strong>major infrastructure, energy, nuclear, rail, defence or other highly regulated capital programmes</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working on projects with significant levels of <strong>cost and schedule uncertainty</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience developing or reviewing <strong>Monte Carlo risk models</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using quantitative risk analysis tools such as <strong>Safran, Primavera Risk Analysis, @RISK, ARM or similar</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience producing and interpreting <strong>P-values, confidence levels, S-curves, tornado diagrams and risk distributions</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with risk allowances, contingency setting and probabilistic forecasting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience integrating risk models with project cost and schedule models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working within a mature <strong>Project Controls function</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recognised project management or risk qualification such as <strong>APM, IRM or equivalent</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Membership of a relevant professional body.</p></li></ul><h2>🔹 At CMR</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have a strong culture driven by our 9 Core Principles. We look to build a community of people that share our values and ambitions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re proud that <strong>96% of our team say CMR is a “Great Place to Work”</strong> — a reflection of our supportive culture, focus on people, and drive to do</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/cmrlondon/risk-manager-major-infrastructure-project-london-443455","tags":["Risk Management"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795848012},{"slug":"ops-strategy-manager-de-london-475610","company_name":"iwoca","title":"Ops Strategy Manager - DE","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The company</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Small businesses move fast. Opportunities often don’t wait, and cash flow pressures can appear overnight. To keep going, and growing, SMEs need finance that’s as flexible and responsive as they are.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That's why we built iwoca. Our smart technology, data science and five-star customer service ensures business owners can act with the speed, confidence and control they need, exactly when it's needed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ve already cleared the way for 100,000 businesses with more than £4 billion in funding. Our passionate team is driven to help even more SMEs succeed, through access to better finance and other services that make running a business easier. Our ultimate mission is to support one million SMEs in their defining moments, creating lasting impact for the communities and economies they drive.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3></h3><h3><strong>The team</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Germany is one of iwoca's core markets, with its own Operations teams across Customer Success, Credit Analysis and Collections. The DE Operations Strategy team is the thought partner to those teams. We exist to understand Operations performance, find where Ops adds the most commercial value, and make the changes that get us there. We're a small team with a startup mindset: we challenge assumptions, prototype quickly, pilot in a lean way, and scale what works.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>The role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an Operations Strategy Manager, you'll own some of the most important projects in our German Operations, from defining the problem through to rollout, across the whole customer journey from application to recovery. Projects could include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Better underwriting.</strong> Redesigning how our Credit Analysts work alongside our credit models, so that their judgement systematically improves model decisions rather than working around them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI and automation in Operations. </strong>Using AI to give our teams richer customer context and remove low-value work – for example, cutting the time Account Managers spend preparing for calls, or drafting the first version of routine customer communications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Smarter task distribution. </strong>Rethinking how work is prioritised and split between people and automated processes – from when an Account Manager should call a customer to which customers need a personal conversation at all – so that our teams' time goes where human judgement adds the most value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stronger recoveries.</strong> Using our growing book of defaulted loans to work out which contact strategies, payment arrangements and recovery routes lead to the best outcomes – for iwoca and for the customer.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Whatever the project, you'll ground decisions in evidence: designing and running split tests, doing your own analysis, and working with our Data Scientists to get even more out of our data. You'll work with Operations, Product and Engineering to put changes live, share recommendations directly with Operations leadership and the German management team, and be part of iwoca's wider community of Analysts and Data Scientists.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>The requirements</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Essential:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategy experience.</strong> You've worked in a top-tier strategy consultancy or in a strategic role at a tech or finance company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Analytical foundations.</strong> You have a strong analytical background, through academic qualifications (such as a STEM degree) and professional experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First-principles thinking.</strong> You break complex problems into their core parts, challenge assumptions, and recommend well-reasoned, innovative solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Execution.</strong> You've taken recommendations from concept to execution, with hands-on experience implementing product or process improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Communication.</strong> You distil complex information into clear, engaging messages for a range of stakeholders – from Data Scientists and Operations Managers to C-level.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI leverage.</strong> You use modern tools, including AI, to improve the quality, speed and rigour of your work, while staying responsible for accuracy and outcomes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>German language.</strong> Our customers are in Germany, so German helps day to day – but it's definitely not a requirement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Coding abilities.</strong> You have experience using Python or SQL – either directly or through coding tools like Claude Code. If you haven't coded before, we'd want you to be excited to learn on the job.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operational excellence.</strong> You've driven measurable improvements in a fast-growing operation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experimentation.</strong> You've designed, run and interpreted controlled experiments, including A/B tests, to inform operational or product decisions.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>The salary</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We expect to pay from £75,000 - £90,000 for this role. But, we’re open-minded, so definitely include your salary goals with your application. We routinely benchmark salaries against market rates, and run quarterly performance and salary reviews.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The culture</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At iwoca, we prioritise a culture of learning, growth, and support, and invest in the development of our team members. We value thought and skill diversity, and encourage people to explore new areas of interest, adopt better tools – including AI – and apply sound judgement so our products and decisions improve over time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The offices</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We put a lot of effort into making iwoca a great place to work:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offices in London, Leeds, Berlin, and Frankfurt with plenty of drinks and snacks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Events and community-led groups, including running groups, padel, and monthly ping-pong and pool competitions.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Medical insurance from Vitality, including discounted gym membership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A choice between a dedicated dental plan or a health cash plan that reimburses everyday medical expenses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A private GP service (separate from Vitality) for you, your partner, and your dependents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days’ holiday per year, an extra day off for your birthday, the option to buy or sell an additional five days of annual leave, and unlimited unpaid leave.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A one-month, fully paid sabbatical after four years.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Instant access to external counselling and therapy sessions for team members that need emotional or mental health support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3% Pension contributions on total earnings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An employee equity incentive scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous parental leave and a nursery tax benefit scheme to help you save money.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Electric car scheme and cycle to work scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Two company retreats a year: we’ve been to France, Italy, Spain, and further afield.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">And to make sure we all keep learning, we offer:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A learning and development budget for everyone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company-wide talks with internal and external speakers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to learning platforms like Treehouse.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Useful links:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://coda.io/@iwocauk/iwoca-benefits-policies-uk"><u>iwoca benefits &amp; policies</u></a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferre