a's four offices in London, Leeds, Berlin and Frankfurt, and the events that keep iwocans connected across them. The team is led by the Office &amp; Community Manager, who is based in London.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The London office is iwoca's largest, and home to teams from across the business. It's busiest midweek, when most teams come in together.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll run the office day to day: the weekly Ocado order within budget, deliveries, post (including to remote staff), supplies and merchandise, and the office Soldo card, reconciled each month. You'll walk the office each week, fix small issues yourself and escalate larger ones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll manage the office's facilities, building and running a planned preventative maintenance (PPM) schedule. You'll find, schedule and supervise contractors — plumbers, electricians and HVAC engineers — be the day-to-day point of contact for our cleaning, equipment and plant suppliers, and look after everything from the coffee machines to the Billi taps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll keep the office safe and compliant. You'll be the primary fire marshal and first aider, carry out and log monthly water hygiene (legionella) and emergency lighting checks, and keep the first aid kits stocked.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll welcome guests, clients and candidates, work with the building reception team on access and security, resolve meeting room clashes, and support the Office &amp; Community Manager on projects like office moves and fit-outs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll help iwocans in London feel part of iwoca — lead the weekly Tuesday office tour for new joiners, run the monthly "Stars of the Month" recognition programme, mark anniversaries and life events, and plan in-office events, Town Halls and socials with the wider Office team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The requirements</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Essential:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have at least two years running the day-to-day of an office or front of house, including ordering, deliveries and visitors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're confident with planned maintenance, building compliance and health and safety — ideally somewhere fast-paced — and you've held contractors and suppliers to what they agreed to deliver.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You use AI tools like Claude or Gemini to get admin done faster — drafting supplier emails, tracking stock, reconciling spend — and you check what they produce before it goes out.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> You've run office projects end to end — a move, a fit-out, a new supplier rollout — both on your own and as part of a wider team, and can talk us through one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have been the person who spots what isn't working in an office and sorts it. You can talk us through examples.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable unpacking deliveries, setting up for events and moving supplies of up to 15–20kg.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You hold first aid or fire marshal certificates. If not, we'll train you when you join.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have managed company expenses on Soldo or a similar platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have an IWFM qualification or equivalent.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The salary</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We expect to pay from £30,000 to £35,000 for this role. But, we're open-minded, so definitely include your salary goals with your application. We routinely benchmark salaries against market rates, and run quarterly performance and salary reviews.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The culture</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At iwoca, we prioritise a culture of learning, growth, and support, and invest in the development of our team members. We value thought and skill diversity, and encourage people to explore new areas of interest, adopt better tools – including AI – and apply sound judgement so our products and decisions improve over time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The offices</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We put a lot of effort into making iwoca a great place to work:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offices in London, Leeds, Berlin, and Frankfurt with plenty of drinks and snacks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Events and community-led groups, including running groups, padel, and monthly ping-pong and pool competitions.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Medical insurance from Vitality, including discounted gym membership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A choice between a dedicated dental plan or a health cash plan that reimburses everyday medical expenses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A private GP service (separate from Vitality) for you, your partner, and your dependents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days’ holiday per year, an extra day off for your birthday, the option to buy or sell an additional five days of annual leave, and unlimited unpaid leave.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A one-month, fully paid sabbatical after four years.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Instant access to external counselling and therapy sessions for team members that need emotional or mental health support