&lt;h3&gt;(Publications or Medical Affairs)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;London ,Manchester, Macclesfield, Glasgow, Hybrid or UK remote&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The power of three of the world&#39;s leading medical communications companies – Nucleus Global, ApotheCom and Ashfield MedComms – and the specialised services and skills within MEDiSTRAVA combine to form iNIZIO Medical. With over 2,000 employees globally, iNIZIO Medical creates compelling content and engage communities across the spectrum of healthcare. We improve scientific understanding and pioneer new ways of partnership, with a united vision to lead and define the future of medical in drug development and commercialisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to continuing growth within iNIZIO Medical we have some fantastic opportunities to join our teams across Nucleus Global, ApotheCom and Ashfield MedComms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Medical Writer with opportunities across multiple therapy areas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role would suit an experienced Senior Medical Writer. It will provide a great career development opportunity for you with the support of a very experienced team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to a Scientific Director, you will develop scientific expertise in assigned therapeutic areas, supporting delivery for a versatile team. Core deliverable tasks include researching and developing technical materials, ensuring that a candidate or employee makes all outputs follow written brief, makes them accurate in content and editorial style, and references them. You will also communicate with clients and KOL on content development and attend scientific meetings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To succeed you will have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Several years experience working within a medical communications agency environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· An academic background in the life sciences (Bachelor of Science, Master of Science, Doctor of Philosophy)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a great compensation package including pension, life insurance, private healthcare and paid time off. In addition to our benefits package, we are happy to talk flexible working with hybrid and remote working options available. We offer excellent opportunities for career and personal development, including opportunities to transfer your skills to our other agencies globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Pledge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to promoting a culture of diversity, inclusion and belonging where everyone can bring each facet of themselves to work each day. We believe that strength in diversity and inclusivity is a driver of our success. We strive to accelerate the adoption and adherence of new medicines across the globe. We&#39;re determined to advance scientific understanding and pursue health equity for all. Inizio Medical is part of Inizio, a strategic partner for health and life sciences with a full suite of medical, marketing, advisory and engagement services.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t meet every job requirement? That&#39;s okay! Our company is dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive, and authentic workplace. If you&#39;re excited about this role, but your experience doesn&#39;t perfectly fit every qualification, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right person for this role or others.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://i.imgur.com/UuLTAa2.png&quot; alt=&quot;disability confident committed&quot; width=&quot;311&quot; style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/apothecom/senior-medical-writer-london-428155","tags":["Scientific & Editorial Services"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1795838122},{"slug":"staff-research-engineer-bristol-cambridge-london-8126","company_name":"Graphcore","title":"Staff Research Engineer","description":"&lt;h1&gt;About the job&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Turn AI research ideas into experiments that help shape Graphcore’s next generation of AI hardware.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Research Engineer in Graphcore Research, you’ll help shape complex projects from hypothesis to evaluation. You can join the team in Bristol, London or Cambridge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our research spans efficient training and inference, numerics, reinforcement learning, and more. You’ll build implementations and algorithms that scale and explore how choices in model design and execution affect hardware efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your work will help to push AI models past the frontier, while turning the results of your work into recommendations that silicon and software engineers can use in their designs. You will explain to various groups which trade-offs matter as models grow and where bottlenecks emerge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also prepare papers and present findings at AI conferences and specialist workshops.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;The team and culture&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Researchers across Bristol, London and Cambridge shape projects around shared research interests. You might work with colleagues to investigate how a model scales,&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;trace a distributed inference bottleneck, or develop an algorithm that enables training with more efficient number formats.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Research team bring a customer perspective and experience making models and software work on Graphcore’s stack at scale. Together, the teams develop ideas in efficient compute, model scaling and distributed training and inference.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore Research works with research groups around the world and publishes at venues including NeurIPS, ICML and ICLR.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A PhD or equivalent experience in a technical discipline such as mathematics, statistics, computer science, physics or chemistry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python skills with a framework such as PyTorch or JAX, with experience in model design, optimisation, evaluation and scaling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to design, run and evaluate machine learning experiments and turn results into clear, actionable reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing low-level code for hardware efficiency and reasoning about threads, caches, compute engines and memory bandwidth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical understanding of deep learning software stacks, including compilation, kernel fusion, framework operators, streams and asynchronous execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of providing technical leadership on complex work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also value applied skills in calculus, probability and linear algebra, or publications at leading AI conferences. Experience training frontier language models or training across large accelerator clusters is strongly desired.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. We also welcome engineers returning to the profession after a career break, including through returnship routes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible working:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Balance your work and personal life with greater flexibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous leave:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Take time to rest, recharge and enjoy life outside of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retirement planning support:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Up to 5% matched pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Phantom equity:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Share in Graphcore’s success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workplace experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Enjoy thoughtfully designed office spaces for collaboration, with free food and an on-site barista to support your day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Peace of mind protection:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Income protection and life assurance to provide financial security for you and your loved ones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Electric Vehicle Scheme:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Choose an electric vehicle and lease it through salary sacrifice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Tailor your benefits package with a choice of additional options, including private medical insurance, cycle to work scheme and dental cover&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome people from all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer and recognise that everyone brings different strengths and perspectives. If you need any adjustments during the interview process, just let us know - we’re happy to support you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Sponsorship&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have the legal right to work in the UK. Unfortunately, we are unable to provide visa sponsorship or support visa applications for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Access to controlled technology&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Some roles at Graphcore involve access to technology subject to U.S. export control regulations. Depending on the role, we may need to assess whether export authorisation is required, taking account of factors such as work location, citizenship and immigration status. Where authorisation is required, this may affect whether or when you can start the role. We’ll explain any relevant requirements during the recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Join the Team at Graphcore&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore is one of the world’s leading innovators in Artificial Intelligence compute. It is developing hardware, software and systems infrastructure that will unlock the next generation of AI breakthroughs and power the widespread adoption of AI solutions across every industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the SoftBank Group, Graphcore is a member of an elite family of companies responsible for some of the world’s most transformative technologies. Together, they share a bold vision: to enable Artificial Super Intelligence and ensure its benefits are accessible to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore’s teams are drawn from diverse backgrounds and bring a broad range of skills and perspectives. A melting pot of AI research specialists, silicon designers, software engineers and systems architects, Graphcore brings together deep expertise to solve complex problems and deliver meaningful progress in AI compute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Want to lead research that turns model-scaling bottlenecks into design recommendations for future AI hardware? Apply today.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/graphcore/staff-research-engineer-bristol-cambridge-london-8126","tags":["Research"],"job_types":[],"location":"Bristol; Cambridge; London","created_at":1795838120},{"slug":"specialist-business-process-sox-and-internal-controls-london-201369","company_name":"Volta","title":"Specialist, Business Process SOX and Internal Controls","description":"<h2><strong>About Volta</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Volta is the category-defining, fully vertically integrated AI infrastructure platform – from capital to clusters to software, under a founder-led enterprise. Our mission is The Utility of Compute™: AI infrastructure as dependable and available as electricity, for every organization that needs it. Launched with a $10B strategic partnership with one of the leading frontier AI labs, a Series A led by Andreessen Horowitz, and a $5B AI Infrastructure Fund, Volta is building the infrastructure layer of the AI era from the ground up. We are 100+ people across London, Palo Alto, and New York, with rapid growth expectations to hundreds.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the Role </h2><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The key responsibilities for the role are as follows:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the Senior Manager, Business Process SOX and Internal Controls on the following activities:</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Timely completion of Process design work for the allocated processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Preparation for the close meetings with process owners and the HODs/CFOs and obtain agreement on gaps, remediations and key controls</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Liaison with the ITGC SOX team to understand the full control landscape (aspects such as SODs, IUCs, Joiners and Leavers etc.)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perform internal, s302 and s404 management control testing ensuring timely completion of testing work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Documentation of the design and testing results (in process maps, RACMs and testing template)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Effective change management to ensure that process maps and RACMs are kept up to date</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Preparation of the SOX SteerCo and Audit Committee updates</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide training and guidance on SOX requirements and controls to the control and process owners</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the internal design, testing and remediation logs up to date</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Timely completion of the design and testing work for allocated processes to the highest quality standards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remediation support by providing pragmatic recommendations which are practical to implement and meet the requirements of the Sarbanes Oxley Act</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>ESSENTIAL COMPETENCIES &amp; EXPERIENCE</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> 2-3 years’ experience of working on SOX programmes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> Big 4 experience preferable (although not mandatory)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> Strong knowledge of the requirement of the Sarbanes Oxley Act</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> Proficiency in using process mapping tools (i.e. MS Visio, GRC tools etc.)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> Effective communication skills (written, verbal, and presentation) with the ability to communicate, challenge and influence in a constructive manner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> Collaborative, team player with positive attitude, and a flexible attitude to work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> Strong project management skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> Proven experience of communicating and engaging across multiple departments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> Open to international travels</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">REQ- 256</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Volta, we believe people do their best work when they feel supported, trusted and able to grow. We're building a company where you can make an impact, keep a healthy balance between work and life, and build a career you're proud of. <br />As a global team, we do our best to provide great benefits wherever you're based. While some benefits vary by country due to local regulations, we believe looking after our people is simply the right thing to do.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary based on the work you do here, not your previous salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity in Volta, giving you the opportunity to share in the company's long-term success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Retirement/pension contributions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive health, wellbeing and insurance benefits</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous number of vacation days each year</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Additional Information</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Background Checks</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">All offers of employment at Volta are conditional on the satisfactory completion of pre-employment screening, which includes confirmation of your right to work, verification of your employment history and a criminal record check, where this is permitted by local law. Screening is carried out by Zinc, an accredited third-party provider, after an offer is made and all information is handled confidentially and in accordance with applicable data protection law.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Equal Opportunity</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Volta is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team and make employment decisions based on skills, qualifications, experience and business needs. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, veteran status or any other legally protected characteristic.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Accessibility</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Volta is committed to providing an accessible recruitment experience for all candidates. If you require accommodations or adjustments at any stage of the application or interview process, please contact us at <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="Hyperlink SCXW200826348 BCX0" ---------- We will work with you to identify reasonable accommodations that enable you to participate fully in the hiring process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Candidate Privacy Notice</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">By applying, you consent to the processing of your personal data for recruitment purposes in accordance with applicable data protection laws, including the UK GDPR, EU GDPR and relevant US state privacy regulations. Your data will be shared only with those involved in the hiring process and will not be used for unrelated purposes. For details, see our Recruitment &amp; Candidate Privacy Notice.<br /></p><h3><strong>Note to Recruitment Agencies</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Volta does not accept unsolicited CVs or candidate profiles from recruitment agencies. Any unsolicited submissions, including those sent directly to hiring managers or employees, will be treated as the property of Volta. No agency fees will be payable unless a valid, signed recruitment agreement is in place, and the agency has been specifically engaged for the relevant vacancy.</p><hr><p>Compensation: £65K – £75K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus</p><ul><li>United Kingdom • £65K – £75K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/volta/specialist-business-process-sox-and-internal-controls-london-201369","tags":["Legal"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London, UK","created_at":1795837386},{"slug":"interim-financial-controller-london-441396","company_name":"Ultralytics","title":"Interim Financial Controller","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Ultralytics:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://ultralytics.com/">Ultralytics</a>, we commit to relentless innovation in the AI space and seek <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://www.ultralytics.com/about">team members</a> who resonate with our ambition to produce the world's best <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://ultralytics.com/yolo">YOLO AI models</a>. If you're obsessed with AI, eager to make an impact on the world, and thrive in dynamic, high-intensity environments, we invite you to apply for a position on our team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🌍 Join the team powering the future of vision AI</strong><br /><strong>Hello, hola, 你好, こんにちは, नमस्ते, hallo, bonjour!</strong> Thanks for stopping by — we know your time is valuable, so here's what makes Ultralytics special.<br /><br /><strong>⚡ Who we are</strong><br />At <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.ultralytics.com/">Ultralytics</a>, we're on a mission to <strong>simplify AI for everyone</strong>. As the creators of the world's leading open-source <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics">Ultralytics YOLO models</a>, we empower millions of developers, researchers, and companies worldwide to build state-of-the-art computer vision applications.<br /><br />Following our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.ultralytics.com/news/ultralytics-raises-30m-series-a"><strong>$30M Series A round</strong></a>, we're expanding rapidly across our global hubs in <strong>London, Madrid, and Shenzhen</strong>. Our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.ultralytics.com/">Ultralytics Platform</a> brings data, annotation, training, deployment, and monitoring together for vision AI teams.<br /><br />We move fast. We build boldly. We execute with purpose. And we do it together.<br /><br /><strong>💼 About the role</strong><br />As <strong>Financial Controller</strong>, you'll own day-to-day accounting and reporting for a <strong>nine-month fixed-term cover</strong>. You'll run the monthly finance cycle end to end across our US, UK, and Spain entities, keeping accounting complete, accurate, and on schedule.<br /><br />You'll join a small finance team, working hands-on from day one and directly with senior leadership. Your work will give the finance lead capacity to focus on the year-end audit and ERP change, while you support audit readiness, fundraising preparation, and the transition to a new system.<br /><br />This role suits an experienced, qualified accountant who can quickly take ownership, work independently with a limited handover, and bring care and clarity to a growing global business.<br /><br /><strong>🚀 What you'll do</strong><br /><strong>Month-end close and reporting</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the US, UK, and Spain month-end close, including journals, accruals, prepayments, and balance sheet reconciliations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare multi-currency group consolidation and monthly management accounts with clear variance commentary.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Complete bank reconciliations and maintain weekly cash positions and forecasts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide accurate, timely figures for investor and board reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain the close checklist, audit-ready support files, SaaS revenue recognition, and deferred revenue schedules.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reconcile intercompany balances and recharges across entities.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Payroll and daily finance operations</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run US payroll through Gusto and UK and Spain payroll through PayFit; reconcile payroll to the general ledger and resolve queries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Process supplier invoices and scheduled payments, following approval limits and dual-authorization controls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reconcile supplier statements, support customer invoicing and credit control, and follow up overdue invoices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Onboard suppliers, verify bank details, and answer finance questions from new starters and other teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate with tax advisors on timely US, UK, and Spain filings, and document finance processes and controls.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Audit, fundraising, and ERP support</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare audit files, lead schedules, and reconciliations; respond promptly to auditor requests and sample queries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support statutory accounts and adjustments ahead of year-end audit fieldwork, mainly in Q1 2027.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the Head of Finance on Series B fundraising readiness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the QuickBooks-to-AI-native ERP change through data cleansing, migration, chart-of-accounts mapping, UAT, and parallel runs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Document new processes and support the team through go-live.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>🧠 Skills and experience</strong><br /><strong>Core requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualified accountant (ACA, ACCA, or CIMA) with at least three years running month-end close and management accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with multi-currency accounting and multi-entity consolidation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on payroll and accounts payable experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience preparing for and supporting an external audit.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to start quickly, work independently with limited handover, and communicate clearly with senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Right to work in the UK.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ERP implementation or migration experience, including data migration, chart-of-accoun