!</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a <strong>Product Marketing Director</strong>, to join the <strong>Product Marketing</strong> team in <strong>France, </strong>for a fixed-term contract (CDD) of 8 months, from February to September 2027, as a maternity leave replacement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Product Marketing Director, you will be in charge of 4 business or product segments: the Consultation Assistant Product, the PRM (Patient Relationship Management) suite product line, the PLG (Product Led Growth) acceleration, and the Dentist market.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With your team, you will define and implement action plans to maximize growth, retention, satisfaction and usage. Your 2 north stars KPIs will be NPS and ARR. You will be the voice of our +100,000 healthcare professionals. You will work with various teams at Doctolib on a day-to-day basis: Product, Design, Marketing, Sales, Ops, Data…</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be part of the Doctolib French leadership team, work directly with Exco members, reporting to the VP Growth, and leading a team of 4 experienced and amazing people. You will have a strong leadership role internally to implement a culture of User &amp; Product centricity, while delivering strong business impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role of Product Marketing at Doctolib includes the following missions:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Market &amp; Customer Insights</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the <strong>voice of the customers</strong> by conducting research on doctors' needs, pain points, and behaviors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor <strong>market dynamics and competitor movements</strong> to provide strategic recommendations for maintaining market advantage, or suggest partnership and M&amp;A</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product prioritization &amp; discovery</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Product Management (PM) to identify and capitalize on <strong>market gaps and opportunities:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring strong convictions on what products are needed to create value and usage</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support PM in the related work during 1/ product building (discovery &amp; delivery) and 2/ product prioritization</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product Positioning &amp; Narrative</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop &amp; own the <strong>positioning strategy on the French market</strong>, that differentiates our solutions vs all alternatives</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define our <strong>product offer, pricing &amp; packaging</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create &amp; maintain powerful <strong>value prop &amp; messaging frameworks</strong> that resonate with target personas</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Usage &amp; Satisfaction</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor and analyze <strong>product usage and satisfaction metrics</strong> to identify opportunities for increased adoption &amp; engagement by doctors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and execute strategies to improve doctors’ <strong>satisfaction and reduce churn</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with PM to<strong> translate usage insights</strong> into product improvements and feature adoption campaigns</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth plan</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design comprehensive <strong>go-to-market strategies with 360° launch plans</strong>, to reach our yearly growth plan (FR budget, in Gross ARR and Net ARR)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor<strong> key business KPIs</strong> (# clients &amp; penetration ; net &amp; gross MRR incl. leads, meetings and CVR ; growth profitability) to ensure growth of the doctors market segment and design right Sales Ops &amp; Marketing actions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure successful execution of launches and campaigns through <strong>360 coordination</strong> with Product, Growth Marketing, Brand &amp; Content, Public Affairs, Legal, Sales Ops and Customer Support teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Brand &amp; Content Marketing to develop <strong>impactful campaigns and content</strong> that support product launches and adoption and increase doctors <strong>satisfaction</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Global Product Knowledge to <strong>support product training on the French market</strong></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Before you read on: if you don't have the exact profile described below, but you feel this job description matches your skill set, we still encourage you to apply.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You could be our next team mate if:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are fluent in <strong>French and English</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have <strong>10+ years of relevant experience,</strong> with a proven track record of <strong>delivering GTM/product positioning strategies</strong> end-to-end, from go-to-market design to execution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have successful <strong>experience of managing and leading a senior team</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong <strong>stakeholder management </strong>skills and can align Product, Sales, Marketing, and Data teams in a fast-moving, complex environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are highly <strong>action-oriented, structured, data-driven</strong>, and comfortable working on a multi-segment scope from day one.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Now, it would be fantastic if you:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have experience in a SaaS or tech product environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are curious about AI and willing to upskill your team on AI-powered product marketing approaches</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free comprehensive health insurance (basic package) for you and your children</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days of paid vacation per year, plus up to 14 days of RTT</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free mental health and coaching services through our partner <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Moka.care">Moka.care</a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work from abroad for up to 10 days per year thanks to our flexibility days policy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch vouchers (Swile card) worth €8.50 per working day, with €4.50 covered by Doctolib</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A subsidy from the work council to refund part of the membership to a sport club or a creative class</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">50% reimbursement of your public transport subscription</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ParentCare Program: Enjoy full salary coverage (100%) during your first month of birth leave and 75% during the second, covered by Doctolib</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">For caregivers and workers with disabilities, a package including an adaptation of the remote policy, extra days off for medical reasons, and psychological support</p></li></ul><h2><strong>The interview process</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30’ remote interview with Talent Acquisition</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">60’ remote interview with the current Product Marketing Director, leaving in maternity (Charlotte Saglier)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">60’ case study with Charlotte Saglier and Julie Touyarot (VP Growth, hiring manager) (ideally onsite but flexible)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final interview with a senior stakeholder (optional)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least one reference check</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Job details</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fixed term contract (CDD 8 months)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full Time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Workplace: Levallois (HQ) or any other location in France (with frequent travels to HQ: once a week in the first 3 months, and then every 2 weeks)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid mode: 3 days of on-site presence per week (or less if outside of Paris: see above)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Start date: February 2027</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compensation : fix + bonus on objectives (according to your profile)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At Doctolib, we are committed to improving access to healthcare for everyone. This translates into our recruitment process. We evaluate candidates based solely on qualifications and motivation, without any form of discrimination.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>The more diverse ideas are heard, the more our product will truly improve healthcare for all. You are welcome to apply to Doctolib, regardless of your gender, religion, age, sexual orientation, ethnicity, disability.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>To ensure equal opportunities, we invite you to exclude personal information (e.g. pictures, age) from your applications. If you require any accommodation, please let us know for support during the hiring process.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us in building the healthcare we all dream of!</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>All information provided is processed by D