><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have worked on a project involving machine learning, natural language processing, or large language models</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have used agentic frameworks like Langchain or Google ADK.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have experimented with AI APIs, prompting, retrieval, or conversational interfaces</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have experience in taking products to production and supporting them with real users.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have some experience with Git, APIs, testing, or data analysis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have an interest in healthcare, privacy, or responsible AI</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Life at Doctolib Tech</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our products are built on a cloud-native platform that supports web and mobile applications across several countries and healthcare systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Even if Doctolib uses technologies like Ruby on Rails, TypeScript, Java, Kotlin, Swift, React Native, and many cloud-related technologies, the principal language you'll work on is Python.You will also have the opportunity to use AI-assisted development tools within our engineering practices.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discover our AI vision<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://careers.doctolib.com/ai-careers/"> here</a> and learn more about our tech culture on the<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://careers.doctolib.com/tech-doctolib/"> Doctolib Tech site</a>.</p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A structured internship with dedicated mentoring</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity to work on real AI projects in a healthcare environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical learning sessions and access to internal engineering communities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to AI tools for coding, development, and learning</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meal vouchers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free breakfast in the office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Up to 2 days of remote work per week</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A flexible workplace policy, depending on the team and location</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative and international working environment</p></li></ul><h2><strong>The interview process</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coding Game</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruiter Interview</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical Interview</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Behavioral Interview</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Job details</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Internship, 6 months, full-time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Location: Berlin, Paris, Nantes, Milan, or Amsterdam</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid work setup, up to 2 remote days per week</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Start date: March 2027</p></li></ul><h2><strong>We welcome everyone</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Doctolib, we are committed to improving access to healthcare for everyone. We evaluate candidates based on their qualifications, motivation, and potential, without discrimination.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The more diverse ideas are heard, the better our products can serve patients and healthcare professionals. We welcome applications regardless of gender, religion, age, sexual orientation, ethnicity, disability, or place of origin.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To support an inclusive recruitment process, we invite you to leave personal information such as pictures and age off your application. If you require an accommodation during the interview process, please let us know.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in building the healthcare w