height:1.5em"><strong>[OUR JOURNEY] </strong>Founded in 2016 and launched in 2017 by<strong> </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/aprot/"><em><strong><u>Alexandre</u></strong></em></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/steveanavi/"><em><strong><u>Steve</u></strong></em></a><em><strong>,</strong></em> Qonto has grown to 1,700 Qontoers serving over 750,000 customers across 8 European countries. We have been profitable since 2023, and we are just getting started.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>[OUR BELIEFS] </strong>We hire for skills and potential. With 80+ nationalities, 45% women, and 56% of women in our leadership team, diversity isn't a program; It's who we are. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/qonto-way/a-recruiters-dilemma-confronting-bias-in-hiring-b78acce148eb"><em><strong><u>We've built a discrimination-free hiring process</u></strong></em></a> because the best teams are built on merit.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>[AI AT QONTO] </strong>AI is deeply embedded in how we work (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/qonto-way/ai-at-qonto-vision-statement-725a7e2f659b"><em><strong><u>here</u></strong></em></a>)<em> - </em>Every Qontoer gets unlimited access to the best AI tools. We want people who experiment without waiting for permission, push AI beyond the obvious, know when to trust it, and when to question it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us as our <strong>Legal Intern – Corporate and M&amp;A</strong> to get hands-on exposure to high-stakes M&amp;A deals and corporate governance work inside one of Europe's fastest-scaling fintechs.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the Legal Intern – Corporate and M&amp;A, you'll have a 360° legal view of Qonto's corporate and M&amp;A activity. You'll work closely with Djesia, our Head of Legal for Corporate, Governance and M&amp;A, and partner regularly with Finance, People, Risk, Regulatory, Compliance, Internal Control, and Strategic Projects teams.<br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support day-to-day general corporate matters, including preparing shareholders' meetings and board meetings</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Draft and monitor BSPCE documentation, including periodic allocation tracking for employee equity schemes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute across the full M&amp;A lifecycle, from audit to closing, drafting transaction documents such as share purchase agreements, investment agreements, shareholders' agreements, and ancillary documents</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help build and improve internal legal processes and tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Carry out legal research on corporate matters and support the Legal team's daily activity</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ What we're looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience:</strong> a prior internship or apprenticeship in an international law firm, bank, or fintech, with real exposure to droit des sociétés and M&amp;A work specifically, not just adjacent corporate or compliance tasks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Academic background:</strong> Master's student in Corporate/Business Law in France; being enrolled at a Bar School (EFB or equivalent) for a January start, a dual degree with a business school or Sciences Po, or an international LLM are all a plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Communication and rigor:</strong> strong oral and written communication, good diplomacy, and solid organizational and analytical skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mindset:</strong> curious, adaptable, proactive and reliable — you take ownership of what's assigned to you and know when to flag something up rather than sit on it; comfortable using AI tools day-to-day</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Languages:</strong> French and fluent English required</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Starting date:</strong> July 2027</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ What we can offer you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work in a fast-paced, scaling legal team at the center of Qonto's corporate and M&amp;A activity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join diverse, inclusive teams across 80+ nationalities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on exposure to live M&amp;A deals, not just observation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to digitalized legal tools (AI-enabled) to support your daily work</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ Your future manager</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work closely with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/djesia-meziani">Djesia</a>, Head of Legal – Corporate/M&amp;A. Djesia has spent 15+ years advising French and international clients on complex domestic and cross-border transactions, acting as lead counsel on M&amp;A, LBO and strategic corporate matters at Dentons and Franklin Law Firm, including a secondment as M&amp;A Senior Legal Counsel at TotalEnergies. Her approach: manage deals end-to-end with pragmatic, business-oriented advice, and lead with rigor while mentoring the team along the way.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Perks</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flex schedule.</str