 Finance, Strategy and our Product teams, and have regular exposure to Qonto’s senior leaders and founders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Evaluate opportunities:</strong> prepare financial analyses and memos on M&amp;A opportunities and strategic questions, including whether Qonto should acquire a company or invest internally to build.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support deal execution:</strong> work with Philippe and the wider team on transactions, helping coordinate timelines, documentation and stakeholders to keep processes moving.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Contribute to investor relations and capital activities:</strong> support Julie on investor communications, reporting, and financing work, including materials that articulate Qonto’s equity story.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Rethink how the team works with AI:</strong> identify opportunities to use AI in M&amp;A and investor relations, and help design and implement processes that improve the team’s work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner across Qonto:</strong> collaborate with Corporate Development, Finance, Strategy, and Product colleagues to turn complex financial and strategic questions into clear, actionable insights.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ What we’re looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience:</strong> You have approximately 4–6 years of relevant experience, for example in investment banking, M&amp;A, private equity, transaction-focused consulting, corporate development in tech or fintech, or a chief of staff role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI fluency:</strong> You have experience applying AI to relevant work and are excited to rethink processes, experiment and use these tools to improve how the team operates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Transactional foundations:</strong> You understand the basics of M&amp;A, fundraising or related transaction work and have practical exposure to deals or due diligence. You’re ready to contribute without starting from scratch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Financial and analytical skills:</strong> You can build and work with financial models, assess opportunities and turn your analysis into clear, well-structured memos and recommendations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Investor relations:</strong> You’re familiar with the fundamentals of investor relations or corporate development and are keen to work across both investor relations and M&amp;A, rather than focus exclusively on transactions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Autonomy and communication:</strong> You’re a self-starter who follows through without waiting to be prompted. You communicate confidently, collaborate with different stakeholders and are comfortable constructively challenging ideas.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Languages:</strong> Fluency in English is required. Another European language is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ What we can offer you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team and scope:</strong> Join a small multicultural team working at the intersection of M&amp;A and investor relations, with a view of both how Qonto deploys capital and how it raises it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact and exposure:</strong> Contribute to important capital allocation decisions and work with experienced colleagues, with regular exposure to senior leaders and founders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ways of working:</strong> Help shape the team’s processes with AI, bringing ideas and initiative to how corporate development and investor relations work gets done.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A defining moment:</strong> Join Qonto just after we obtained our banking licence, as we enter a new chapter and progressively expand the lending and savings solutions we offer businesses across Europe.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ Your future manager</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your manager will be <strong>Lionel Blache</strong>, our <strong>VP, Corporate Development, Investor Relations and Strategic Partnerships</strong>.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>His background?</strong> Lionel built Qonto’s corporate development and investor relations functions, led a secondary transaction, and executed the acquisition and integration that launched Qonto’s first accounting products. Previously, he worked in technology investment banking at Rothschild &amp; Co, advising on cross-border M&amp;A and financing transactions, and held roles operating alongside founders, in technology M&amp;A and transaction advisory.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What does he bring to the team?</strong> Lionel brings experience across capital strategy, M&amp;A and investor relations, combining an operator’s perspective with a background in financial transactions. He’s looking for a self-starter who can contribute autonomously in a small team and help rethink its processes with AI.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>[DIVERSITY]</strong> <em>At Qonto, we understand that true diversity isn’t just about ticking boxes on a hiring checklist. Apply regardless of the boxes you tick - who knows? You may have the missing piece of the puzzle we’ve been searching for all along.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>[HIRING PROCESS DURATION]</strong> <em>On average, <strong>our hiring process lasts 20 working days. </strong>More information on our candidate journey </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://qonto.com/en/careers/candidate-journey"><em><strong><u>here</u></strong></em></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>[DATA RETENTION]</strong> <em>By applying, you agree that Qonto processes your personal data to assess your application. Your data is kept for up to 2 years in our candidate pool. Read our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://qonto.com/en/legal-documents/privacy-notice"><em><u>Privacy Notice</u></em></a><em> for full details.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🔒 Your security matters to us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruitment scams are on the rise. Qonto will never work with third-party platforms or agencies that request payment from candidates. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Qonto, please report it to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/qonto/corporate-development-manager-paris-69522","tags":["Finance & Strategy"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris, France","created_at":1795848011},{"slug":"senior-ai-engineer-paris-215372","company_name":"Qonto","title":"Senior AI Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>[OUR MISSION AND CUSTOMERS] </strong>We are creating the freedom for SMEs to succeed by delivering Europe's leading finance workspace with banking at its core, augmented by financial tools. We are proud to be <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.trustpilot.com/review/qonto.com"><em><strong><u>rated 4.7 on Trustpilot,</u></strong></em></a><em><strong> </strong></em>based on 60,000 reviews. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://qonto.com/en/careers/culture"><em><strong><u>Our culture</u></strong></em></a><em><strong> </strong></em>puts customer satisfaction at the core of what we do <em>(more about our culture </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/qonto-way/the-qonto-way-our-culture-is-our-strategy-90defd4895f9"><em><strong><u>here</u></strong></em></a><em>).</em></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>[OUR JOURNEY] </strong>Founded in 2016 and launched in 2017 by<strong> </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/aprot/"><em><strong><u>Alexandre</u></strong></em></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/steveanavi/"><em><strong><u>Steve</u></strong></em></a><em><strong>,</strong></em> Qonto has grown to 1,700 Qontoers serving over 750,000 customers across 8 European countries. We have been profitable since 2023, and we are just getting started.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>[OUR BELIEFS] </strong>We hire for skills and potential. With 80+ nationalities, 45% women, and 56% of women in our leadership team, diversity isn't a program; It's who we are. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/qonto-way/a-recruiters-dilemma-confronting-bias-in-hiring-b78acce148eb"><em><strong><u>We've built a discrimination-free hiring process</u></strong></em></a> because the best teams are built on merit.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>[AI AT QONTO] </strong>AI is deeply embedded in how we work (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/qonto-way/ai-at-qonto-vision-statement-725a7e2f659b"><em><strong><u>here</u></strong></em></a>)<em> - </em>Every Qontoer gets unlimited access to the best AI tools. We want people who experiment without waiting for permission, push AI beyond the obvious, know when to trust it, and when to question it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us as an AI Engineer in our AI Products team to make sure the AI agents we ship are as reliable as they are fast to build. You'll design the evals, observability and tooling that keep agent quality high in a regulated bank.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build agents:</strong> You'll develop agents that take real actions for customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Match rigor to risk:</strong> You'll size evaluation to the stakes, because an agent making transfers is not a PR bot.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own evaluation of every feature:</strong> You'll make sure every new agent capability comes with the right evaluation strategy, defining what needs to be tested offline and validated online, based on business requirements, expected outcomes and risk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Observe agents in production:</strong> You'll build the monitoring strategy that makes agent behaviour visible, tracks performance against business objectives and flags issues early.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scale it as a platform:</strong> You'll turn our tools, evaluation practices and monitoring capabilities into a self-service platform that lets other teams build, evaluate and operate their own agents.<br /><br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ What we're looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Evaluation mindset:</strong> You've evaluated models or LLM systems and know what makes a test misleading.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong ML foundations:</strong> You understand the ML lifecycle, from training and iteration to evaluation and monitoring, and core concepts such as overfitting, generalization and cross-validation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>LLM and agentic systems knowledge:</strong> You understand the fundamentals of LLMs (particularly the Transformer architecture) and the building blocks of agentic systems. You know how to optimize an agent's harness (prompts, tools, hooks and orchestration) to improve its reliability and performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Builder instinct and backend comfort:</strong> You've built and shipped something used by real users, whether professionally, during an internship or as a side project. You're comfortable reading and writing backend code, working with APIs and integrating systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-native curiosity:</strong> You follow developments in AI closely, experiment with new approaches on your own and use AI tools daily in your work.<br /><br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ What we can offer you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A rare problem:</strong> You'll make AI agents trustworthy in a regulated bank, where quality is not optional.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on coaching:</strong> You'll learn directly from Pierre-Jean, one of the AI engineers in the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Room to grow:</strong> Your scope grows as the platform opens to more teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Space to experiment:</strong> You'll work at the frontier of AI in a team that keeps experimentation at its core.<br /><br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ Your future manager</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your manager will be <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sophie-cornay-16101a23/">Sophie Cornay</a>, our Product Leader for AI Products.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Her background?</strong> Sophie has led product teams in startups and established tech companies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What does she bring to the team?</strong> She gives engineers real ownership and space to experiment.<br /><br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>➡️ Our stack and practices</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Python and Pydantic-ai:</strong> Python is our baseline language, and Pydantic-ai is our agentic framework.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AWS:</strong> We access our models through AWS.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grafana:</strong> We track usage and cost per sub-agent on it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>GitHub and CI:</strong> Every agent change ships through a reviewed pull request.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Braintrust:</strong> Evaluation and agent monitoring run on our self-hosted instance.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>[DIVERSITY]</strong> <em>At Qonto, we understand that true diversity isn’t just about ticking boxes on a hiring checklist. Apply regardless of the boxes you tick - who knows? You may have the missing piece of the puzzle we’ve been searching for all along.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>[HIRING PROCESS DURATION]</strong> <em>On average, <strong>our hiring process lasts 20 working days. </strong>More information on our candidate journey </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://qonto.com/en/careers/candidate-journey"><em><strong><u>here</u></strong></em></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>[DATA RETENTION]</strong> <em>By applying, you agree that Qonto processes your personal data to assess your application. Your data is kept for up to 2 years in our candidate pool. Read our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://qonto.com/en/legal-documents/privacy-notice"><em><u>Privacy Notice</u></em></a><em> for full details.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🔒 Your security matters to us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruitment scams are on the rise. Qonto will never work with third-party platforms or agencies that request payment from candidates. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Qonto, please report it to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/qonto/senior-ai-engineer-paris-215372","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris, France","created_at":1795848011},{"slug":"lead-architect-digital-assets-tokenization-paris-340971","company_name":"Ant-Tech","title":"Lead Architect – Digital Assets & Tokenization","description":"<p>Location: Paris, France (4 days onsite per week)</p><p>Employment Type: Permanent, Full-time</p><p>Salary: €100,000 – €120,000 gross/year</p><h2>About the Opportunity</h2><p>We are partnering with a leading European financial market infrastructure group to build a new Digital Assets division, focused on tokenisation and Distributed Ledger Technology (DLT).</p><p>The mission is to develop next-generation financial infrastructure, launch innovative digital asset products for institutional and retail clients, and bridge traditional finance (TradFi) with decentralised finance (DeFi).</p><p>This is a unique founding-style leadership opportunity within an established, highly regulated financial institution. You will have the opportunity to shape the technical vision, own the architecture, and build foundational technology from the ground up.</p><h2>The Mission</h2><p>You will lead the architecture of the organisation's first tokenised financial products, covering two major initiatives:</p><ul><li>Tokenised Securities Platform: Building an issuance, trading and settlement platform for equities, ETFs and bonds, featuring 24/7 trading, fractional ownership and on-chain Delivery-versus-Payment (DvP) settlement.</li><li>Tokenised Collateral Management Platform: Enabling real-time repo transactions, CCP margin eligibility and DeFi distribution of government bonds through regulated lending environments.</li></ul><p>Your responsibility is to translate these strategic initiatives into secure, scalable and auditable technical architectures.</p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><ul><li>Own end-to-end architecture for digital asset solutions, integrating DLT with traditional financial market infrastructure, including trading, clearing, settlement, custody and CSD.</li><li>Design cross-chain architectures across permissioned networks (Hyperledger Besu, Canton Network) and public blockchains (Ethereum/L2).</li><li>Define on-chain compliance frameworks, including ERC-3643/T-REX token standards, KYC-whitelisted wallets, AML screening and transaction reporting.</li><li>Architect institutional custody and key management solutions using MPC technologies such as Fireblocks and Taurus.</li><li>Establish engineering standards covering code quality, architecture reviews, testing and secure-by-design development.</li><li>Lead threat modelling and security architecture for high-value financial systems.</li><li>Drive build-versus-buy decisions across blockchain infrastructure, custody and audit solutions.</li><li>Collaborate with Product, Engineering, Legal, Regulatory, Clearing and CSD stakeholders.</li><li>Remain hands-on with critical technical components and high-risk incidents.</li><li>Build and develop the engineering team as the platform transitions from development to production.</li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul><li>7+ years of experience in Solution Architecture, including at least 3 years working on DLT or blockchain projects.</li><li>Strong expertise in distributed systems and blockchain architecture.</li><li>Hands-on experience with EVM and permissioned blockchain networks such as Canton or Hyperledger Besu.</li><li>Knowledge of regulated security token standards, particularly ERC-3643/T-REX or equivalent.</li><li>Strong understanding of smart contract security, cross-chain risks and on-chain compliance.</li><li>Experience designing secure, highly available financial systems operating 24/7.</li><li>Working knowledge of capital markets infrastructure, including DvP, CSD, CCP and settlement processes.</li><li>Strong leadership skills with a player-coach mindset.</li><li>Excellent communication skills and ability to work with technical and non-technical stakeholders.</li><li>Degree in Computer Science, Engineering or a related field.</li></ul><h2>AI Engineering Skills (Required)</h2><ul><li>Experience defining AI-augmented software development workflows using coding assistants, smart contract scaffolding and AI-generated test suites.</li><li>Ability to establish governance and security guardrails for AI-assisted code, including code reviews, secret management and licence/provenance checks.</li><li>Experience evaluating AI development tools and identifying practical productivity improvements.</li><li>Understanding of AI-powered product capabilities such as anomaly detection and operational triage, including associated risk controls.</li></ul><h2>Why Join?</h2><ul><li>Take ownership of the architecture for a major digital asset infrastructure initiative.</li><li>Build innovative tokenisation products at the intersection of TradFi and DeFi.</li><li>Work within an established European financial institution while enjoying the autonomy of a zero-to-one project.</li><li>Influence strategic technology decisions and shape the future engineering team.</li></ul><p>Important: Candidates must be willing to work onsite in Paris, France, 4 days per week.</p><p>Salary: €100K–€120K gross annually.</p><p>#Blockchain #DigitalAssets #Tokenization #DLT #SolutionArchitect #FinTech #DeFi #TradFi #AIEngineering</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/ant-tech/lead-architect-digital-assets-tokenization-paris-340971","tags":["Software Development"],"job_types":["Permanent contract (cdi - contrat à durée indéterminée)","manager"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1795842029},{"slug":"manager-i-engineering-language-platform-paris-446877","company_name":"Datadog","title":"Manager I, Engineering - Language Platform","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.datadoghq.com/tracing/&quot;&gt;Application Performance Monitoring&lt;/a&gt; (APM) is one of Datadog’s premier products that helps developers see inside complex distributed systems. Our SDKs are both the delivery vehicle for APM and the platform on which all of Datadog’s service and app based products (e.g. Application Security Management, Profiling, Data Stream Monitoring…) are delivered. We believe our SDKs are one of our technical moats and are a key competitive advantage for APM and Datadog more broadly. They’re also open-source.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leading the evolution of our SDKs is a technically demanding and highly collaborative effort. You’ll work with language experts to deliver cutting-edge observability products across our 9 supported languages, with industry leading performance and a world class developer experience. You’ll rethink our SDKs’ architecture, APIs, data models, and protocol to meet Datadog’s current needs and scale, all while building in the open. And you’ll grow your team’s capacity by fostering a culture focused on customer needs, continuous learning, and innovation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced Engineering Manager who cares as much about technical excellence as empowering other engineering teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships that it builds, the creativity it brings to the table, and the collaboration of being together. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our employees can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, grow, and develop a team of roughly 4-8 library engineers — coaching, giving direct feedback, and empowering senior ICs as technical leaders owning outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own team delivery and productivity: planning, milestones, reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product teams to:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reshape and grow our platform capabilities to enable product teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and deliver industry leading, open-source, zero-touch APM instrumentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay technically close to the work — apply strong technical judgment, set a high standard for quality, contribute code where it matters most, and keep quality and architecture high&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships and drive alignment across the language teams and product, backend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape team identity and culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An experienced Engineering Manager with a track record of shipping&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong and empathetic leader with the ability to build and lead high-performing teams to deliver high quality software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability pivot from high level product narratives to highly technical implementation details&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have significant programming experience in one or more of: Go, C, Rust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bonus&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt; If you possess experience with one or more of these skills: systems programming experience, observability tooling experience, experience shipping client side software, Go runtime expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your skills, we encourage you to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits and Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New hire stock equity (RSUs) and employee stock purchase plan (ESPP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous professional development, product training, and career pathing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intradepartmental mentor and buddy program for in-house networking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An inclusive company culture, ability to join our Community Guilds (Datadog employee resource groups)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to Inclusion Talks, our Internal panel discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free, global mental health benefits for employees and dependents age 6+&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive global benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits and Growth listed above may vary based on the country of your employment and the nature of your employment with Datadog.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: white;&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Datadog:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog is the leading observability and security platform for the AI era, providing businesses with unified visibility across the technology stack to manage complexity at scale. It brings applications, infrastructure, data, models, and security into one place, using AI to detect and resolve issues before they impact customers. Trusted globally by Fortune 500 companies and high-growth AI leaders, Datadog enables businesses to move faster with clarity and confidence. Learn more about #DatadogLife on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/datadoghq/?hl=en&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/datadog&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn,&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://learn.datadoghq.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Datadog Learning Center. &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;215&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Equal Opportunity at Datadog:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog is proud to offer &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12ScreenRdr.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;equal employment opportunity&lt;/a&gt; to everyone regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, veteran status, and other characteristics protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements. Here are our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/candidate-legal-notices/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Legal Notices&lt;/a&gt; for your reference.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
