tranger ;</p></li><li><p>Identifier et extraire des informations de multiples sources en utilisant une grande variété d’outils de recherche ;</p></li><li><p>Organiser, synthétiser et interpréter ces informations, sous la supervision du Business Intelligence Manager (BIM) ou des Managers, Principals et Partners ;</p></li><li><p>Assurer la mise à jour et l’optimisation des outils du capital intellectuel (base documentaire, présentations standards, profils consultants, abonnements base de données…)&nbsp;</p></li></ul> <br> <p>Etudiant(e) d’une Grande École de Commerce ou d’Ingénieur, vous êtes dynamique et avez déjà une expérience dans un environnement exigeant et rigoureux. Vous disposez d’une excellente capacité d’analyse et de synthèse. Méticuleux(se), rigoureux(se) et doté(e) d’un réel esprit d’équipe, vous avez démontré un sens du service extrêmement développé.</p><p>Un anglais courant, à l’écrit comme à l’oral, est indispensable.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/advancy-partners/paris-stagiaire-assistant-equipes-conseil-h-f-386962","tags":["Consultants"],"job_types":["Entry","internship"],"location":"Paris, Île-de-France, France","created_at":1795816284},{"slug":"procurement-excellence-manager-paris-148138","company_name":"Mistral.ai","title":"Procurement Excellence Manager","description":"<h2><strong>About Mistral</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral provides full-stack AI solutions: from frontier models to developer tools, applications, and compute. We partner with enterprises tackling the hardest problems across high-stakes industries like finance, manufacturing, defense, healthcare, and the public sector, co-creating customized AI systems that they can run on their terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a dynamic, collaborative team passionate about AI and its potential to transform society. Our diverse workforce thrives in competitive environments and is committed to driving innovation. Our teams are distributed between Europe, North America, Asia and the Middle East. We are creative, low-ego and team-spirited.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Procurement Excellence Manager on the General Procurement team, reporting to the Procurement General Lead, you will be the engine of procurement operational excellence at Mistral AI. Working closely with category managers, buyers, Legal and Finance, you will drive and measure the performance of the whole procurement function and turn it into a data-driven organization: coordinate end-to-end processes (procurement, legal review, P2P and Payflows operations), build the performance framework and reporting, and deploy AI agents to automate day-to-day procurement tasks. You define and execute the procurement excellence roadmap for your scope, with direct visibility from Finance leadership, in a function being built from scratch at a hyper-growth AI company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Define the KPI framework</strong> of the procurement function (savings, cycle times, process compliance, policy adoption, project pipeline) and run regular performance reviews</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build dashboards</strong> to steer costs and team activity from P2P and finance tool data, and produce reporting for the Procurement Lead, FP&amp;A and Finance leadership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run spend analysis and ensure data quality</strong> (categorization, supplier master data) to support category strategies and supplier panel performance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Map and harmonize end-to-end processes</strong> across procurement, legal and P2P, and remove bottlenecks on purchasing files</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run Payflows operations</strong>: approval workflows, P2P/finance tool integrations, billing data reliability and reconciliation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive onboarding of business units</strong> to the purchase process and the P2P tool in successive waves, with training, communication and change management; maintain procurement playbooks and support the policy roll-out</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support compliance topics</strong> in partnership with Legal (code of conduct, anti-bribery, purchasing conditions)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Specify, build and deploy AI agents</strong> to automate recurring procurement tasks (requester support, first-level need analysis, standard contract drafts, supplier follow-ups, spend data extraction and cleansing), leveraging Mistral's internal AI tooling, and measure their impact (time saved, quality, adoption)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we're looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 5 years of experience in procurement operations, process excellence, data/analytics or P2P tool management, ideally in a fast-scaling environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong data-driven mindset: you design KPI frameworks, dashboards and spend analyses and make processes measurable</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with P2P/ERP tools and process digitization (workflow design, integrations, data quality)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience deploying automation or AI agents in an operational context, and eager to leverage Mistral's internal AI tooling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent project and stakeholder management skills to align Procurement, Legal, Finance, IT and business units across entities