 of the Digital Natives team based in Europe. You will own deals end to end, from first conversation through production launch and expansion, working alongside our solutions engineering, product, science, and legal teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is based in London, with regular travel across the region and to our Paris headquarters.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You Will Do:</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pipeline development (targeted outbound and qualified inbound):</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify and engage the most promising AI-native companies in your territory, and build relationships with the founders and engineering leaders who select models</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualify and convert inbound interest from teams already building on our API into commercial relationships</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical evaluation:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guide customers through evaluations of our models on their real workloads, working with our solutions engineers to keep the process fast and the results clear</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn successful evaluations into production usage and long-term commercial agreements</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deal management and closing:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the commercial cycle end to end: qualification, evaluation, negotiation, and close, together with our legal and solutions teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage deals with multiple technical and executive stakeholders on both sides, and keep everyone aligned on timelines and next steps</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Account growth:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow usage within existing customers as they ship new products and features on our models</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay close to customers' roadmaps so Mistral is positioned for their next workload before it reaches production</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Working with product and science:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring customer feedback, usage patterns, and competitive insight back to our product and science teams to inform priorities and the roadmap</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Connect customers directly with our product and research teams where it accelerates their success</p></li></ul><h2>What We're Looking For:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5 to 8 years of sales experience, with a track record of closing deals with startups and scale-ups for a technical product (API, developer tools, infrastructure, or data)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling to technical buyers: founders, CTOs, and engineering leaders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of how AI products are built, and the ability to hold a credible conversation about models, evaluation, and deployment with an engineering audience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience at a fast-growing startup, ideally in AI, developer tools, or infrastructure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with usage-based revenue, where growth comes from what customers ship rather than from a single contract</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent English and French</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong negotiation and communication skills, and a hands-on, low-ego approach</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being, growth, and work-life balance. Benefits vary by country and may include healthcare coverage, parental leave, retirement plans, relocation support, wellness programs, meal and transportation allowances, and other location-specific perks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For the most up-to-date details on benefits available in your location, please refer to our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://app.notion.com/p/mistralai/Benefits-at-Mistral-36e6ba59a7fe836b93dd01737fcc27ef?source=copy_link">Benefits page</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Privacy Policy</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your privacy matters to us. You can learn more about how we handle your personal data in our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://legal.mistral.ai/terms/applicant-privacy-policy"><u>Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/mistralai/account-executive-digital-natives-paris-426986","tags":["Business"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1795815614},{"slug":"ma-equity-financing-legal-counsel-paris-174768","company_name":"Mistral.ai","title":"M&A & Equity Financing Legal Counsel","description":"<h2><strong>About Mistral</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mistral provides full-stack AI solutions: from frontier models to developer tools, applications, and compute. We partner with enterprises tackling the hardest problems across high-stakes industries like finance, manufacturing, defense, healthcare, and the public sector, co-creating customized AI systems that they can run on their terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a dynamic, collaborative team passionate about AI and its potential to transform society. Our diverse workforce thrives in competitive environments and is committed to driving innovation. Our teams are distributed between Europe, North America, Asia and the Middle East. We are creative, low-ego and team-spirited.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role Summary </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our <strong>M&amp;A &amp; Equity Financing Legal Counsel</strong>, you will work directly under the Head of M&amp;A and Finance Legal Counsel, based in Paris. In close collaboration with our Business and Finance teams, you will play a key role in structuring, drafting and negotiating <u>Mistral’s external growth transactions and equity fundraisings.</u></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Mistral operates at the frontier of AI, where the pace of innovation demands transaction execution speed and precision that match the technology itself. You will help shape the growth and business relationships that will define Mistral’s next chapter.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Draft, negotiate and advise on a wide range of M&amp;A transactions, including acquisitions, acqui-hires and other internal or external growth projects worldwide.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take an active part in every stage of M&amp;A transactions: deal structuring, due diligence, negotiations, signing and closing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate the process for Mistral’s equity fundraisings, including legal communication with prospective investors, structuring the company's due diligence disclosure, drafting investment documentation and leading the signing and closing of equity fundraisings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate and assist on Mistral’s secondary sale transactions on behalf of investors and employees.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Draft