rategies</strong> with marketing and sales, including pricing, positioning, and adoption plans.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Align stakeholders</strong> across engineering, design, and business teams around priorities, trade-offs, and timelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Prioritize ruthlessly</strong> to maintain a dynamic roadmap that delivers quick wins while advancing long-term initiatives.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of <strong>Product Management experience</strong> in competitive, ambiguous environments, ideally with generative AI, LLMs, or ML-driven products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical acumen</strong> to understand trade-offs and partner effectively with engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>User obsession</strong> with a relentless focus on solving real problems, supported by data and qualitative insights.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-functional influence</strong> to align and inspire teams without direct authority.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Problem-solving skills</strong> that balance big-picture thinking with hands-on execution, from roadmap crafting to metrics analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clear communication</strong> with persuasive storytelling for executives, teams, and users in docs, decks, or whiteboard sessions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Adaptability</strong> to thrive in dynamic settings where priorities shift quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaborative mindset</strong> with low ego and high EQ, building trust and driving decisions through clarity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Autonomy</strong> to navigate unknowns and own outcomes end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Gro