 detection concepts, and equipment selection</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Specify and verify safety functions to ISO 13849 (PL) and IEC 61508, including safety requirement specifications and validation reports</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compliance and technical documentation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compile and maintain technical construction files, CE Declarations of Conformity, type-approval dossiers and certification reports</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and review user, installation, operation and maintenance manuals, safety instructions and labelling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain the standards register and assess the impact of new or revised standards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage certification change control: assess design changes for impact on existing certificates</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaboration and continuous improvement</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the internal authority on certification scope: ensure in-service conformity of series production with certified designs, and support procurement and supply chain on material and packaging compliance (e.g. RoHS, packaging regulations).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support design reviews and supplier qualification, including component certificates (ATEX, PED, electrical)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Standards and regulatory scope</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role covers, but is not limited to, the frameworks below. Working knowledge of most is expected; deep expertise in several is required</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">IEC 62282 series, CSA/ANSI FC 1:2021, ISO 16110-1 and Machinery Regulation (EU) 2023/1230</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><h1><strong>Required qualifications</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Master’s or bachelor’s degree in mechanical, electrical, chemical, process or safety engineering, or equivalent</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in product certification, compliance or safety engineering for complex electromechanical or process equipment (energy, gas, process, machinery or marine)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct experience with hydrogen or fuel cell systems and the IEC 62282 series, CSA/ANSI FC 1 or ISO 16110</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of taking products through CE marking and third-party certification with notified bodies or NRTLs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience leading FMEA, HAZOP and risk assessments, and documenting them to auditor standard</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid knowledge of ATEX / IECEx, hazardous area classification and explosion-protection concepts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience specifying and validating safety functions to ISO 13849 and/or IEC 61508</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent technical writing: clear, structured, audit-ready technical files and manuals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English, written and spoken</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><h1><strong>Preferred qualifications and personal profile</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Marine type approval with a classification society (DNV, LR, BV, ABS) or IGF Code projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with fuel processing, reformers or fire equipment, and with pressure equipment under PED</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Certified functional safety qualification or ATEX/IECEx competence certification</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with North American