&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/artefact/ai-architect-zurich-26850","tags":["AI Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1795805729},{"slug":"drone-system-validation-engineer-intern-lausanne-40767","company_name":"Harmattan Ai","title":"Drone System Validation Engineer Intern","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>About the Role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Drone System Validation Engineer Intern, you will own one well-defined validation topic for six months within our Validation team in Paris or Lausanne. Your topic is agreed during the interview process and fitted to your profile. You will work hands-on with our autonomous drone systems across simulation, lab, bench and flight testing. The team uses your work directly as it scales its test activities, and strong performers have a natural path to a full-time Validation Engineer role.<br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scope your validation topic and agree on a plan and deliverables with the team in your first month.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare and run flight and bench test campaigns, including setup, execution and issue reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analyze flight logs and telemetry to explain system behavior and find the root cause of anomalies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and improve test procedures so campaigns stay consistent across sites and teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share findings with Flight Operations, Automated Testing, GNC and embedded software teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay in constant touch with the validation team and iterate on their feedback, then document, hand over and present your results at the end.<br /></p></li></ul><h3><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final-year engineering or MSc student in aerospace, robotics, mechatronics, electronics, embedded systems or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to complete a six-month end-of-studies internship under an agreement with your school.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on project experience (student drone, rocket or robotics team, lab project, internship), ideally testing or debugging physical systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rigorous test mindset: you check results, question surprises and trace issues to their root cause.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Autonomous and able to turn a loosely defined brief into a concrete result.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborative team player who is comfortable with outdoor field days in all weather.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/harmattan-ai/drone-system-validation-engineer-intern-lausanne-40767","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1795804814},{"slug":"terrain-following-and-collision-avoidance-intern-lausanne-362561","company_name":"Harmattan Ai","title":"Terrain Following and Collision Avoidance Intern","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are developing advanced autonomous systems that need to fly close to the ground, over varied terrain and through cluttered environments such as forests and built-up areas, where there is very little margin for error.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Even a carefully prepared flight plan must be backed by onboard sensing, ready to react to terrain variations and unexpected obstacles. We are building this capability and exploring hybrid approaches that combine planning and real-time reaction.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your mission</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The goal of this internship is to explore, develop and evaluate terrain-following and collision-avoidance methods based primarily on onboard sensors, enabling safe low-altitude flight.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Literature review</strong>: Conduct a comprehensive review of existing terrain-following approaches and obstacle-avoidance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Algorithm Implementation</strong>: Develop and implement various algorithms based on the literature review and project requirements using simulated and real-world flight data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Performance evaluation:</strong> Assess and compare the performance, safety margins and computational overhead of the developed algorithms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Embedded constraints:</strong> Ensure the solutions are compatible with real-time execution and the computational limits of onboard hardware.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Documentation:</strong> Document all work performed, including methodologies, results, and conclusions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flight Tests Participation</strong>: Actively participate in flight test sessions to gather real-world data and validate the effectiveness of the developed algorithms in operational conditions. Contribute to real-time deployment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Candidates Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Educational Background:</strong> A strong academic record in robotics, aerospace engineering, automatic control, applied mathematics or a related field. Knowledge of perception, guidance or motion planning is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Skills:</strong> Solid foundation in sensor fusion and/or guidance  and control. Experience with lidar or vision processing, terrain data or drones is a major plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mindset:</strong> You are curious to learn, autonomous and able to take initiative.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/harmattan-ai/terrain-following-and-collision-avoidance-intern-lausanne-362561","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1795804814},{"slug":"flight-control-intern-stabilizing-unstable-aircraft-lausanne-448305","company_name":"Harmattan Ai","title":"Flight Control Intern - Stabilizing Unstable Aircraft","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Flight Control Intern, you explore how far an aircraft can be pushed beyond natural stability, and what performance that buys. Instability makes aircraft more agile, but only if the control system can keep them flying. You own your project end to end: you choose and build unstable airframes, identify their dynamics from flight data, design the control that stabilizes them, and measure the limits of what can be achieved. You work on agile, high-performance platforms in a fast-paced engineering team with an industrial, production-first mindset, flying frequently on a dedicated test range. You are a full member of the team, with visibility on how the company and its products evolve and a direct impact on what we ship.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong><br />Select and justify unstable configurations to study, such as multirotor and VTOL (vertical take-off and landing), relaxed-stability fixed wings, and tailless, blended-wing or canard layouts.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and build the airframes yourself (foam, 3D printing, composites), integrate the avionics provided by the team, and repair after crashes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and run flight test campaigns with excitation maneuvers, and iterate quickly on a dedicated test range.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify the aircraft dynamics from flight data (system identification) and validate the models against analytical and simulated results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and tune stabilizing controllers on PX4 or ArduPilot, then port them to Harmattan's in-house flight controller firmware.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Push the instability step by step, for example by moving the center of gravity aft or reducing control surfaces, and analyze stability margins.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Quantify the performance envelope, including the limits set by actuator bandwidth, sensor noise and latency, and the agility gained in return.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a reusable toolchain: a Python simulation workflow (for example JSBSim or Gazebo) validated on flight data, hardware-in-the-loop tests, flight test procedures and a data analysis pipeline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Present concepts, results, and project status to the team and to wider audiences, and join team meetings to learn from other projects.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Currently pursuing an MSc in Aerospace Engineering, Control, Robotics, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid foundations in flight mechanics and control theory, ideally with experience in system identification or stability analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in Python. C/C++ and embedded firmware experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on building experience, such as RC aircraft, drones, or any fabrication project. Familiarity with PX4 or ArduPilot is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with flight testing, debugging in the field, and learning from the occasional crash.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Motivated, autonomous, and proactive, with the ability to own a project and communicate results clearly.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/harmattan-ai/flight-control-intern-stabilizing-unstable-aircraft-lausanne-448305","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1795804814},{"slug":"gnc-engineer-intern-robust-rl-lausanne-300382","company_name":"Harmattan Ai","title":"GNC Engineer Intern - Robust RL","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a GNC Intern, you will join a team that has spent several months building AI-based guidance, navigation and control tools. Your mission is to understand where our AI control model is strong and where it breaks, then make it robust enough for the demands of high-speed flight. You will work at the interface between advanced theory and real-world application, from overnight training runs to flight test days.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Literature Review: Conduct theoretical and applied literature reviews on the robustness of AI models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Model Diagnostics: Apply the most relevant methods to study our control model and diagnose its weaknesses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Training Strategies: Set up targeted training strategies to strengthen the model against extreme operating conditions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experimentation &amp; Analysis: Launch and analyze training runs, documenting results to guide subsequent iterations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Benchmark Performance: Improve performance on control benchmarks compared to the existing model.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tooling &amp; Embedded Integration: Develop new tools within the training framework and streamline model integration onto embedded systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flight Testing &amp; Data Processing: Prepare hardware, support live flight tests, and post-process collected data.