&lt;li&gt;Experience creating reusable technical frameworks, demos, or enablement that scale across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/databricks/delivery-solutions-architect-zurich-116421","tags":["Field Engineering - FE Invested DSA"],"job_types":[],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1795794924},{"slug":"head-of-hardware-zurich-56355","company_name":"Microagi","title":"Head of Hardware","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Accelerating embodied AGI.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The next ten years of AI will not be won in software. They will be won in the physical world: in factories, hospitals, kitchens, fields, and homes. The companies that own that data will own the century.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">microagi is building it. We are a data research and deployment lab. <strong>Atlas</strong> captures the manual work inside Europe’s industrial champions, trains foundation models on it, and deploys the right robot onto the floor, with no teleoperation and no interruption to the line. <strong>Shift</strong> records how physical work actually happens and turns it into training-ready data.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We were founded by former Formula 1 engineers from Red Bull Racing and Mercedes, together with a researcher from the Alan Turing Institute. Our $55M seed round, the largest in German history, was led by Hummingbird with Northzone, LocalGlobe, Village Global, and redalpine. We are based in Munich, with our research centre in Zürich and teams in London, New York, and Istanbul. We are now building the engineering and research teams that will take Atlas into new industries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our models learn from data captured in the physical world, by hardware we design and build ourselves. As Head of Hardware, you own that hardware end to end: electrical, firmware, and the mechanical integration that holds it together, from the first schematic to devices running on factory floors.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You lead the team that builds it. Today that is about six engineers on robotics, three on EMG sensing, and three on camera systems, plus contractors, and it will grow quickly. Our Electrical Engineer and Embedded Engineer roles report to you. You set the architecture they build against, and you still build alongside them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a founder-shaped role, not a management seat. We are looking for someone who has carried a product from a blank page to customers with real skin in the game, wants to build both the thing and the team that builds it, and would rather design than review. If that sounds like you, you will want to do it again at the earliest stage.<br /></p><h2>What You Will Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the hardware roadmap for Shift and Atlas data capture: wearables, sensor rigs, camera systems, and prototype robots. What we build, in what order, and why.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the system architecture across electrical, firmware, and mechanical: sensors, compute, power, wireless, and enclosures. Make the trade-offs, and make them stick when disciplines disagree.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay on the bench: schematics, layout reviews, board bring-up, and a scope in your hands when the team is stuck. On the days it matters, you are the best electrical engineer in the room.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead and grow the team: hire, set the bar, run design reviews, and give engineers ownership of whole subsystems rather than tickets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guarantee data quality end to end: EMG and EEG front ends, camera pipelines, IMUs, and synchronization across many devices, so that what reaches the ML team is clean, time-aligned, and trustworthy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take designs from prototype to small-batch production: DFM, component and EMS vendors, test fixtures, certification, and field reliability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work shoulder to shoulder with ML and deployment. Your hardware decides what the training data looks like, and you will be on the floor where it is captured.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run contractors and partners without losing ownership of the result.<br /></p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have taken at least one product from zero to shipped, with significant ownership of the outcome: as a co-founder, CTO, first hardware hire, or the lead who owned the whole device. Not one subsystem, not one phase. Ideally a wearable, at a tier-one hardware company known for shipping at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Electrical engineering is your home discipline. You have designed boards that shipped, across mixed-signal, power, wireless, and high-speed digital, and you can still do it today.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You think in systems. You understand how an electrode choice, an enclosure tolerance, and an ADC sample rate interact, and you can hold the mechanical and firmware conversations as a peer, not a customer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have led engineers: hired them, grown them, and kept a team shipping through 0-to-1 ambiguity. Typically 6+ years in hardware, but we care more about what you shipped than how long it took.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong understanding of how hardware decisions affect data quality. You know that a great model on a noisy signal still loses to a decent model on a clean one, and you design accordingly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience taking hardware to small-batch production: DFM, vendor and EMS management, test, and certification.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuinely curious about ML: you read papers, you have trained at least one model end to end, and you understand that dataset quality beats model architecture choice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High agency: you don't wait to be told what to do. A 0-to-1 hardware program takes the hours it takes, in person and at pace, and you have chosen that before.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discreet: you handle confidential hardware roadmaps and customer data with care.<br /></p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wearables, smartwatches, drones, robotics, AR/VR, or defense wearables on your résumé.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Camera systems: sensor selection, MIPI and ISP pipelines, and multi-camera synchronization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Low-power and battery design, BLE or Wi-Fi, and antenna integration in small enclosures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enough mechanical fluency (CAD, tolerances, and materials) to challenge the mechanical team’s choices and be right some of the time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prior founder or founding-engineer experience, including the parts that went wrong.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Open-source hardware or firmware contributions.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/microagi/head-of-hardware-zurich-56355","tags":["microagi"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1795794013},{"slug":"mitarbeiter-garantie-und-lieferantenmanagement-100-dielsdorf-46261","company_name":"NYDEGGER Personal/Engineering AG","title":"Mitarbeiter Garantie- und Lieferantenmanagement 100% (m/w/d)","description":"<p>Eintritt: Nach Vereinbarung</p><p>Arbeitsort: Dielsdorf</p><h2>Tätigkeiten:</h2><ul><li><p>Abwicklung von Garantieansprüchen und Lieferantenreklamationen</p></li><li><p>Durchsetzung von Rückforderungen in Zusammenarbeit mit Einkauf und Qualitätsmanagement</p></li><li><p>Analyse von Qualitäts- und Kostenabweichungen sowie Erarbeitung von Optimierungsmassnahmen</p></li><li><p>Erstellung von Auswertungen zur Identifikation von Fehlerquellen und Kostentreibern</p></li><li><p>Erfassung neuer Maschinen und Pflege der ERP-Stammdaten</p></li></ul><h2>Profil:</h2><ul><li><p>Abgeschlossene technische oder kaufmännische Ausbildung mit einer Weiterbildung im jeweils anderen Bereich</p></li><li><p>Mehrjährige Berufserfahrung in einer vergleichbaren Funktion</p></li><li><p>Sehr gute Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse</p></li><li><p>Versierte EDV-Kenntnisse (MS Office, SAP)</p></li><li><p>Sie sind eine kommunikative und durchsetzungsstarke Persönlichkeit mit einer zuverlässigen und strukturierten Arbeitsweise</p></li><li><p>Sie verfügen über eine schnelle Auffassungsgabe und vernetzte Denkweise</p></li></ul><p>Es erwartet Sie eine verantwortungsvolle Aufgabe und ein motiviertes Team.</p><p>Verfügen Sie über die entsprechenden Erfahrungen und arbeiten motiviert und teamorientiert? Dann sind Sie die richtige Person für unseren Kunden und wir freuen uns auf Sie!</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/nydegger-personalengineering-ag/mitarbeiter-garantie-und-lieferantenmanagement-100-dielsdorf-46261","tags":["Quality Management"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag","berufserfahren"],"location":"Dielsdorf","created_at":1795793486},{"slug":"quality-inspector-hengelo-5530","company_name":"Destinusgroup","title":"Quality Inspector","description":"<p><strong>About The Role</strong></p><p>Imagine this - As a <strong>Quality Inspector</strong>, you’re on the production floor, surrounded by state-of-the-art defense aerospace technology — components built to dominate the skies, withstand extreme environments, and empower next-generation defense systems. You’re the last line of defense between cutting-edge innovation and uncompromising reliability. 🚀&nbsp;</p><p>At <strong>Destinus</strong>, we are revolutionizing the defense industry with cutting-edge Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs). Our innovative technologies are designed to meet the unique demands of modern defense operations, delivering unparalleled speed, precision, and cost effectiveness. <strong>Destinus</strong> partners with government agencies and defense organizations worldwide to provide advanced solutions for mission-critical operations, enabling a new era of efficiency and technological superiority. Join us in shaping the future of defense with groundbreaking aerospace innovations.</p><p></p><p><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul><li>Be the Guardian of Quality:&nbsp;Inspect aerospace components, assemblies, and processes to ensure everything is up to spec — no compromises.&nbsp;</li><li>Find and Fix:&nbsp;Identify defects,&nbsp;troubleshoot root&nbsp;causes, and work&nbsp;hand-in-hand&nbsp;with production and engineering teams to solve problems&nbsp;before&nbsp;they take flight.&nbsp;</li><li>Raise the Bar:&nbsp;Help us improve our inspection processes, finding smarter, faster ways to&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;top-tier quality without slowing down progress.&nbsp;</li><li>Document the Journey:&nbsp;Record inspection results and generate reports — because quality&nbsp;isn’t&nbsp;just what we&nbsp;do,&nbsp;it’s&nbsp;what we&nbsp;prove.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><strong>What You’ll Need</strong></p><p><strong>Must-Have</strong></p><ul><li>Proven experience as a Quality Inspector in aerospace, automotive, or high-tech manufacturing.</li><li>Strong understanding of technical drawings, blueprints, and inspection methods.</li><li>Sharp attention to detail — you spot imperfections others miss.</li><li>Knowledge of ISO standards, quality systems, and reporting procedures.</li><li>English and Dutch</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Nice-to-Haves</strong></p><ul><li>Experience with non-destructive testing (NDT).</li><li>Familiarity with Lean Manufacturing or Six Sigma principles.</li><li>Basic understanding of composite materials or advanced alloys.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><p>You’re not just an inspector — you’re a perfectionist with purpose. You thrive in fast-paced, high-stakes environments where every detail matters, driven by curiosity to constantly question how things can be done better, faster, and smarter. You’re a problem solver who doesn’t just spot issues — you dive in, figure out what went wrong, and help make it right. Most importantly, you take ownership, knowing that when you’re part of a team reshaping aerospace defense, you don’t wait for someone else to lead the way — you set the standard.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/destinusgroup/quality-inspector-hengelo-5530","tags":["Production & Manufacturing"],"job_types":["Associate"],"location":"Hengelo, Netherlands","created_at":1795850412},{"slug":"software-engineer-creatives-team-utrecht-212093","company_name":"Channable","title":"Software Engineer - Creatives Team","description":"<h4><span style="color:#121317">What’s in it for you (to start with):</span></h4><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Gross monthly salary ranging from € 3.600 to € 5.700 based on a 40-hour work week. This salary range reflects our career framework. Your final role level will be determined throughout the recruitment process, based on alignment with this framework</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">8% holiday allowance - 8% of your yearly salary, which is paid together with your May salary</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Saving for old age - we have a savings scheme for old age, which can accrue up to 5% of your monthly salary, or you can get an additional +2.5% to your monthly base salary.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#121317">And many more benefits that you can read about at the bottom of the job description!</span></p><h4><span style="color:#121317"><br>Your challenges:</span></h4><p><span style="color:#121317">The Creatives team works on and is responsible for our Image Editor and related image-processing features. <br>You will be working on the backend and sometimes a little bit on the frontend of a complex distributed web application. Our tool provides several different services, written in </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">Haskell, Python, and Rust.</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">In this position, you will be responsible for the architecture, development, and maintenance of new and old image-related features in our application. An important aspect of our work is scaling our services to the next level, so we can handle another order of magnitude increase in throughput while keeping our app fast and responsive. To give you a sense of scale: a couple hundred millions of images are inspected, transformed and created by our services every day.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Plan and shape the future of the Creatives suite of features with our tight-knit team</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Design, develop, and test new product features</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Collaborate with and review PRs of other team members</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Improve the reliability and robustness of our application</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Work on scalability and performance improvements</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Collaborate with our other product and platform teams to integrate image-manipulating features with other parts of our tool.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#121317">Our Stack includes: Haskell, Python, Rust, PostgreSQL, TypeScript, React, Ansible, Terraform, Prometheus. And we run all of our infrastructure on Google Cloud Platform.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="color:#121317">Who are you?</span></h4><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You have good programming skills in Haskell (or a similar typed functional language)</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You are familiar with other programming languages and polyglot programming: we regularly need to make modifications in services written in other languages (especially Python and Rust) as well</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You have at least 1 year of professional software engineering experience&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You have experience in tuning and scaling a big application</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You have experience with web development, web technologies, and APIs</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Familiarity with SQL and relational databases, preferably Postgres</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Good working knowledge of Linux, git, and the command line.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Nice to have: </span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Knowledge of Haskell libraries like warp, conduit, async, servant, aeson, effectful</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Knowledge of Rust and its ecosystem</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Prior experience in image processing</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Some knowledge of TypeScript/React, which we use in our WYSIWYG Image Editor</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A passion to provide value to customers and figuring out the 'question behind the question'.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#121317">Practical requirements:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">EU citizenship or a valid work permit for the Netherlands; you are preferably already living in the Netherlands</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Available for at least 32 hours a week, with two days spent at the Utrecht office.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Important note:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> we understand that studies show women may only apply for roles when they feel they meet 100% of the requirements; therefore, we strongly encourage you to apply even if you don't check every box, as we are looking for passionate individuals with potential and a willingness to grow.</span></p> <br> <h4><span style="color:#121317">The team:</span></h4><p><span style="color:#333333">You will join the Creatives team, consisting of five more Backend engineers, two Frontend engineers, a Product Manager, and a UI/UX designer.&nbsp;</span></p><h4><span style="color:#121317">Who are we?</span></h4><p><span style="color:#000000">Channable was founded in 2014 in the heart of Utrecht and is a fast-growing B2B SaaS platform that offers a fully integrated way to market your products online. We empower marketers and online businesses to manage, scale, and optimize their marketing. We are now a strong team of 320+ diverse individuals from more than 40+ nationalities.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Joining Channable means you’re looking for a bit more than just a job. Diverse as we are, we all share our love for growth, helping, taking ownership, and creating an awesome journey together. Feel free to take a further look at who we are here and on our Instagram or LinkedIn! Wanna get to know us even more? Give our</span><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://online.fliphtml5.com/qtfug/wxhm/#p=1"><span style="color:#1155CC"> Culture Playbook</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000"> a read.</span></p><h4><span style="color:#121317">Why Channable?</span></h4><p><span style="color:#000000">At Channable, you’ll find a culture that values openness, craftsmanship, and collaboration. We invest in our people and give them the autonomy to drive meaningful change. You'll work on technical challenges that matter, with colleagues who care deeply about the product and each other.<br></span></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">Want to read more about our development adventures? Then visit our inspiring tech blog:</span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://tech.channable.com/"><span style="color:#121317"> </span></a><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://tech.channable.com/"><span style="color:#121317">https://tech.channable.com/</span></a></u></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">And if this makes you enthusiastic, you can also take a look at some of our open-source work at</span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://github.com/channable"><span style="color:#121317"> </span>https://github.com/channable</a><span style="color:#121317"> to get a feeling of how we work together and what our code looks like.</span><br></p><h4><span style="color:#121317">More benefits:</span><span style="color:#434343">&nbsp;</span></h4><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Annual L&amp;D budget of €1000 to spend on your professional growth.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Company-wide performance bonus, up to 10% of your annual salary, determined yearly by our founders based on financial planning and targets.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Stock Appreciation Rights: senior employees can financially profit from Channable’s success.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">26 vacation days + 2 reload days based on 40 hours, with the possibility of buying up to 5 extra vacation days per year</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Are you going to become a parent? Enjoy 5 weeks of 100% paid partner leave!</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Commuting to our office? Choose between an NS Business Card or a €0.25/km travel allowance for alternative transport.&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Work from our office in central Utrecht at least 2 days a week, and from home for the rest (we'll provide the gear and a budget for extra supplies). Plus, enjoy flexible working hours with a morning start window between 8:00 AM and 10:00 AM.&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">We offer a 3-week-long workcation; and an additional 3 weeks if you live as an expat in the Netherlands!</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Your well-being matters: we offer a discounted Urban Sports Club subscription and anonymous access to OpenUp psychologists and resources.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Fresh daily lunch: enjoy fresh meals prepared Monday to Thursday by our in-house Chef (fully catering to vegan, vegetarian, and gluten-free diets). On Fridays, we switch it up by ordering in tasty sandwiches and salads.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Additional working conditions include massages, even personal training sessions at our Channagym, video games, an in-office bar, and many more!</span></p></li><li><p><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/channable_channable-channaweek-workculture-activity-7426540961326895105-EXff?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAAASoXJgBHdq4CVsQCH0PpnYcTQNs3ymnPIk"><span style="color:#1155CC">Channaweek</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000"> &amp;</span><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/channable_channaweekend-teambuilding-employee-activity-7472609865060978688-4yrx?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAABZ4BZEBIP93wvMbEFJl-McVwLtU2nhZoao"><span style="color:#1155CC"> Channaweekend:</span></a><span style="color:#1155CC"> </span></u><span style="color:#000000">connect with your global colleagues at our annual team gathering in Utrecht, and pack your bags for Channaweekend, our annual company-wide getaway.&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul><p><br></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#121317">How can you introduce yourself to us?</span></strong></h4><p><span style="color:#121317">Are you interested? To ensure your application reaches the right team quickly, please submit it in English directly through our careers page by clicking the “Apply” button. Applications submitted via email won’t be considered.</span><span style="color:#333333"> </span><span style="color:#121317">We</span><span style="color:#000000"> look forward to hearing from you as soon as possible!</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Interview steps:</span></p><ol><li><p><span style="color:#121317">If it's a match, Ioana (Tech Talent Acquisition Partner)&nbsp; will get in touch with you for an introductory call (25 minutes)</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Then you are going to have a tech interview with the team members (1h)</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">For senior candidates, we schedule a system design as well&nbsp;(1h)</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">After that, we will schedule a culture and role fit interview with the Creative Team Lead and one more colleague (1h)</span></p></li></ol><p><span style="color:#121317">When we don’t have enough information, we might ask you to work on a short assignment before your tech interview. <br>Please note that after the interviews and before the offer stage, we’ll conduct reference checks.</span></p><p><br><span style="color:#000000">Important note: We know that in the current AI era, it's tempting to use technology to polish your interview performance. While we value your ambition, please do not use AI assistance during the first screening,&nbsp; so we can get to know the real person behind the resume.<br></span></p><p><em><span style="color:#000000">Note: Contact from job agencies and recruiters will not be appreciated. Each recruiter or headhunter who approaches us agrees with a donation of €250 to Make-A-Wish.</span></em></p><p><em><span style="color:#000000">At Channable, we strive to create and foster an environment of belonging and collaboration, and we believe in diverse and inclusive teams</span></em><br></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/channable/software-engineer-creatives-team-utrecht-212093","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Utrecht, Utrecht, Netherlands","created_at":1795848684},{"slug":"junior-data-ai-engineer-finance-amsterdam-39987","company_name":"Prosus","title":"Junior Data & AI Engineer (Finance)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who We Are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've ordered dinner through Just Eat Takeaway. You've bought and sold on OLX. You've paid with PayU. Chances are, you've already used a Prosus company today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are Prosus, a global technology company powering some of the world's leading lifestyle ecommerce businesses. Every day, billions of people across India, Latin America, Europe and beyond use our products and services to buy, sell, pay, connect and discover.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our AI-driven ecosystem spans 100+ companies across ecommerce, food delivery, fintech and experiences, serving billions of consumers worldwide. AI powers how we operate and innovate, with more than 60,000 active AI agents helping our teams build, scale and move faster. Through our investment team, we also back the founders and technologies shaping the future: From robotics and autonomous systems to synthetic biology and frontier AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guided by our five values <strong>Innovation, Results, People, Impact, and Entrepreneurship,</strong> culture is our competitive advantage. We thrive with experimentation; we build, we test, we learn, we iterate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in shaping the future of technology at global scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Finance Junior Data &amp; AI Engineer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location: </strong>Amsterdam, Netherlands |  <strong>Duration: </strong>(12 months)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>About the role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Finance AI team sits within the Prosus finance organisation and supports the function in reimagining finance through AI. We partner with finance teams to build and deploy impactful AI transformation projects, at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will join the team as a hands-on Junior Data and AI Engineer. You will help build and maintain the data pipelines that power our AI solutions, and get your first taste of the "intelligence layer" on top: retrieval systems (RAG) and agentic workflows that automate financial analysis. You will work alongside experienced engineers who will guide your work and help you take on more ownership as you grow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It is a practical role with real projects, real data and direct exposure to finance teams who use what we build.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you will do</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>1. Data pipelines and infrastructure</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help build and maintain cloud-based data lake and pipelines using Databricks and following established patterns and team standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help develop efficient data pipelines for ingesting, processing, and storing large datasets, incorporating best practices for data quality, lineage tracking, and metadata management - specifically optimized for LLM consumption.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement data quality checks, monitor pipeline health and help fix issues as they arise.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>2. RAG and agentic workflows</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">RAG &amp; Agentic Systems: Contribute to RAG components (chunking, embeddings, retrieval) and help test improvements such as hybrid search and re-ranking to handle dense financial documents and tables.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agentic Workflows: Help build agent workflows using LangGraph and Databricks Agents, with design guidance from senior colleagues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evaluation: Support the evaluation of AI outputs with "LLM-as-a-Judge" frameworks (MLflow)  to quantify accuracy, faithfulness, and latency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Follow security and privacy guidelines so that AI outputs comply with financial regulations and privacy standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help maintain and document reusable "Agent templates" that empower Finance business partners to build their own safe AI-driven workflows.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>3. Collaboration and enablement</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with AI teams and key stakeholders across finance to understand data requirements for AI systems and ensure their smooth deployment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Document your work and share what you learn with the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help finance colleagues use our tools and templates for data tasks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take part in day-to-day workflows with business functions to ensure prompt and high-quality data movement from source systems to production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Follow security, privacy and data governance guidelines (including GDPR) in everything you build.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you bring</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1-2 years of experience with a focus on data lake and cloud infrastructure, with an interest in GenAI (RAG, agents or LLM-integrated apps).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on exposure to building data pipelines in cloud environments (e.g. AWS, Azure, or GCP). Databricks experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good working knowledge of SQL and Python or another programming language to develop custom automation scripts, tables, and solutions. You should be comfortable using AI-native IDEs like Cursor/claude code to accelerate development and refactoring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with MCP servers to expose databases and local tools to LLMs, and with REST/GraphQL/FastAPI for building the deterministic "hooks" that AI agents call.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A structured, methodical approach to problem-solving and the willingness to learn how to troubleshoot.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communication in English and the confidence to ask questions and work with technical and non-technical colleagues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in the Netherlands with the right to work here.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Nice to have</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of metadata systems and data lineage tracking tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to a cloud platform (AWS, Azure or GCP).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with CI/CD and DevOps practices and infrastructure as code (e.g., Terraform, Ansible).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An affinity for machine learning engineering or an intention to further develop skills in this area.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with data warehousing concepts and platforms like Snowflake, Google BigQuery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A basic understanding of financial concepts and an interest in helping finance colleagues adopt self-service tools.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Prosus?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Prosus, your colleagues include 60,000 AI agents… and your job is to figure out what that actually means. We're one of the largest operators of agentic AI on the planet, inside a $100B+ portfolio across 100+ companies and two billion people. The humans here own what AI can't do alone: judgment, creativity, and the call on what gets built next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Own the impact. Work the ecosystem. Earn your growth. Build with backing.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Curious about our perks and benefits? Take a look </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://prosusbenefits.com/"><em><u>at this page</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Diversity &amp; Inclusion Commitment</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We respect the dignity and human rights of individuals and communities wherever we operate in the world. Building an inclusive workplace where everyone feels welcome and can thrive is critical for us. We provide access to education, which helps everyone understand the important role they play and the positive impact they can have.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Want to know more about life at Prosus? Explore our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.prosus.com/the-prosus-way"><em>culture and values</em></a><em>.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/prosus/junior-data-ai-engineer-finance-amsterdam-39987","tags":["Investment Org. - Finance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795848015},{"slug":"senior-logistics-lead-3pl-management-eindhoven-169286","company_name":"Axelera AI","title":"(Senior) Logistics Lead - 3PL Management","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Position Overview</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.axelera.ai">Axelera AI</a> builds the hardware that brings AI to the edge, and our chips, boards and systems are shipping to customers around the world. Every evaluation kit, sample and production order needs to arrive on time, intact and fully compliant.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our (Senior) Logistics Lead, you will own these logistics at Axelera end to end. You will lead the relationship with our global 3PL partner, from business reviews and KPI management to speaking up when something goes wrong. At the same time, you will stay hands-on: receiving, kitting and dispatching goods for our R&amp;D, test and lab teams. You will have the mandate to shape how logistics works at Axelera and to build processes and systems that scale with our growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Eindhoven, Netherlands. On-site at least 3 days a week (with some flexibility around office presence, e.g. mornings only).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>3PL Partner Management</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Be the single point of contact with our 3PL partner for warehousing and express shipping</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Run regular business reviews, manage KPIs and SLAs, and drive corrective actions</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Escalate and resolve operational issues (delays, damages, losses, stock gaps) with the 3PL and carriers</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Translate Axelera's needs into clear instructions and work procedures for the 3PL</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Check 3PL invoices against agreed rates and keep logistics costs under control</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Evaluate and onboard new logistics partners and services when needed</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Shipment Orchestration</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Plan and release outbound orders for customer deliveries, samples and evaluation kits</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Coordinate inbound flows from suppliers and contract manufacturers</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Manage express shipments with the major carriers: booking, labels, documents and tracking</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Keep customers and internal teams informed on status, lead times and exceptions</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Own the logistics mailbox and make sure every request is handled on time</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Trade Compliance &amp; Customs</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Prepare the right shipping and customs documents for every destination</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Apply correct Incoterms and work with customs brokers and customs on clearance, duties and VAT</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Run export checks, including denied-party and sanctions screening, together with our compliance owner</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Help maintain HS codes and export classifications for our products</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Internal Logistics</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Receive, inspect, store and issue goods at our Eindhoven site</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Kit, pack and dispatch shipments for R&amp;D, test and lab teams, including ESD-sensitive goods</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Move material between Axelera sites, the 3PL and external partners</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Keep storage areas organized, labelled and safe</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Inventory Control &amp; Process Improvement</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Make sure stock at the 3PL and at our sites matches NetSuite, and investigate differences</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Organize cycle counts and the year-end stock count with the 3PL and Finance</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Act as key user for logistics in NetSuite and work with Novutech to automate transactions and integrate 3PL data</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Write clear procedures and find ways to cut cost, lead time and manual work</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Interfaces</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>External: </strong>3PL partner, express carriers, freight forwarders, customs brokers and customs, suppliers and contract manufacturers, customers' logistics teams</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Internal: </strong>Supply Chain and Planning, Sales and Customer Operations, Finance, R&amp;D and test labs, Legal and Compliance</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Qualifications</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Required</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Bachelor's degree in logistics, supply chain or a related field, or equivalent experience</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· 5+ years in logistics operations, ideally in electronics, semiconductors or high-tech, at a senior or lead level</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Proven experience managing a 3PL or logistics provider as a supplier, including business reviews, KPIs and escalations</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Familiarity with export/import documents, Incoterms, HS codes and customs procedures</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Experience with an ERP system (NetSuite preferred) and strong Excel skills</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Structured and proactive, and comfortable switching between managing partners and doing the physical work yourself</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Fluent in English; Dutch at B1 level or higher, enough to deal professionally with customs and local partners in writing/speaking without issues</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Living within commuting distance of Eindhoven</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Preferred</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Knowledge of export control regulations (EU dual-use, US EAR) and sanctions screening</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Experience with ESD-safe handling and shipping dangerous goods such as lithium batteries</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">· Experience with ERP automation or system integration projects</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is your chance to shape and be part of a dynamic, fast-growing, international organization. We offer an attractive compensation package, including a pension plan, extensive employee insurances and the option to get company shares.   </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">An open culture that supports creativity and continual innovation is awaiting you. Collaborative ownership and freedom with responsibility is characteristic for the way we act and work as a team. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At Axelera AI, we wholeheartedly embrace equal opportunity and hold diversity in the highest regard. Our steadfast commitment is to cultivate a warm and inclusive environment that empowers and celebrates every member of our team. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds to join us in shaping the future of AI.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Axelera AI may at times work with external parties (such as recruiters, headhunters, or executive search firms) to support both publicly posted and confidential searches. Our hiring process never involves any payment from candidates, and we will never require you to use a particular paid service to be considered for a role. If you have been approached by someone on our behalf and want to confirm it’s legitimate, please contact us directly at </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="ms-outlook-linkify" ----------<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/axelera-ai/senior-logistics-lead-3pl-management-eindhoven-169286","tags":["Corporate Functions"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Eindhoven (hybrid)","created_at":1795848015},{"slug":"revenue-operations-manager-amsterdam-8571","company_name":"Tebi","title":"Revenue Operations Manager","description":"<h2><strong>About Tebi</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tebi is building a modern connected hospitality operating system that helps entrepreneurs run their business more intelligently and smoothly. In one seamless platform, Tebi embeds sales, reservations, kitchen, inventory, and payments (as well as all the data that powers it) helping to automate work, streamline operations, and give hospitality owners the clarity and time they need to focus on what matters the most: creating great guest experiences.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded by Arnout Schuijff, co-founder of Adyen, and backed by €50 million in funding from Index Ventures &amp; CapitalG, Tebi is build in service of hospitality first. Thousands of restaurants, cafés, bars, and coffee shops across the Netherlands, UK, Spain, Italy, Denmark, Germany, Finland, and Ireland.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a Revenue Operations Manager to build and run the systems behind Tebi’s revenue engine, from how we find and win merchants to how we onboard, retain and grow them across seven European markets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll apply skills like building enrichment flows, tracking buying signals, setting up outbound and automating workflows in HubSpot and the tools around it across the customer lifecycle, from lead enrichment and outbound to onboarding handover, customer health and expansion. You’ll report to our RevOps Lead and work closely with Sales, Marketing, Onboarding, Account Management and the Data team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on role where speed matters. You’ll build with Clay, HubSpot, n8n, APIs, webhooks and AI, and take every idea from first experiment to a system the whole go-to-market team relies on. You understand what drives revenue, so you know what is worth building, and you work in short loops: ship fast, measure, learn and adapt quickly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the acquisition engine</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build enrichment flows, ideal customer profile scoring and lead routing that turn raw leads into clear next actions for reps in HubSpot.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and automate signal tracking across the funnel, including walk-in activity in emerging markets not yet visible in HubSpot.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build outbound plays and sequencing systems for sales-led and PLG motions, and run experiments to learn how best to reach customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prototype and improve an AI outbound assistant that saves reps time, with a human in the loop.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the processes and automation behind onboarding, retention and expansion</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and automate the Sales-to-Onboarding handover process across our toolstack, replacing manual steps and setting milestones, ownership and service levels from signed to live, with alerts when a merchant stalls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set up the retention signals and risk alerts that matter, each routed to a clear action and owner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design the expansion framework from scratch for sales-led (Account Manager-led) and PLG (automated, in-product or lifecycle) upsell, and build the plays, sequences and automation behind it in our toolstack.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Measure and refine these processes against pipeline, retention and expansion outcomes, and talk to reps, Account Managers and merchants about their pain points to turn what you learn into better workflows and systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain the integrations across our toolstack, including HubSpot, BigQuery and the enrichment and outbound tools, and document system logic so it scales with the team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Need</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Around 3 or more years of relevant experience in RevOps, sales operations or customer success operations, or an equivalent role in B2B SaaS.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience building enrichment flows, signal tracking and outbound systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in high-velocity SaaS or an agency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good knowledge of Clay and other GTM tools, such as n8n, Make, Apollo, Instantly or similar, and comfort working with APIs and webhooks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on HubSpot experience beyond admin work: workflows, lifecycle stages, properties and reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience building workflows, sequences and lifecycle automation end to end, for both sales-led and PLG motions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing and automating onboarding or handover processes, and defining health, risk and expansion signals that turn into alerts and actions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to understand customer pain points and translate them into plays and systems that people use in their daily work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Day-to-day experience building with AI, with real workflows, agents or automations you have shipped, and a habit of testing new tools to see what works.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An “everything is figureoutable” mindset: you start from a blank page, ship a first version fast, learn from what happens and adapt quickly.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with BigQuery, Dataform, Metabase or comparable analytics tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">B2B SaaS experience in a growing company where systems and processes are still being built, ideally across multiple countries or markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with hospitality technology, POS, payments or merchant services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience applying AI to outbound and customer success workflows, with attention to data quality and human review.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for an operator who thinks commercially, builds with AI every day and moves fast: building from scratch, learning by testing, and helping every merchant get live quickly and grow with us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this speaks to you we can be the right fit. Learn more about how we work from our Recipe here:<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.tebi.com/gb/careers"> <u>https://www.tebi.com/gb/careers</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Start-up Equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch in the office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible time off</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team events</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What is Restaurant Software?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Restaurants and other merchants use various software systems such as Point of Sale (POS), Reservations, Kitchen Display Systems (KDS), Payments, Inventory, Staffing, and the list goes on. These systems all need to speak to each other which they frequently don’t. It’s a mess, and we are fixing it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From buying a croissant at a cafe to having dinner with friends, it’s a €4 Trillion+ global market and a critical part of everyday life in today's economy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we use AI at Tebi</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use AI the way our merchants use Tebi, to cut out the friction and get to what matters faster. We believe in a world where AI increases quality, efficiency and speed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Tebi, AI isn't a policy or a checkbox, it's just part of how we work. It helps us write, analyse, build, and improve but doesn’t make the last call. If there's a smarter way to do something, we want to find it.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/tebi/revenue-operations-manager-amsterdam-8571","tags":["Success"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795837383},{"slug":"interim-senior-analytics-engineer-powerbi-databricks-leiden-36214","company_name":"Riverflex","title":"[Interim] Senior Analytics Engineer (PowerBI & Databricks)","description":"<p><strong>Job Title: </strong>Senior Analytics Engineer<br><strong>Location:</strong> Leiden, 