cv.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Visser Elektrotechniek &amp; de VDK Groep</h3><p>Bij ons draait alles om slimme totaaltechniek. Al sinds 1919 verzorgen zij elektrotechnische installaties, beveiliging, duurzame energieoplossingen en onderhoud voor uiteenlopende projecten. Met een hecht team van vakmensen werken zij aan betrouwbare en toekomstgerichte oplossingen, waarbij kwaliteit, betrokkenheid en service altijd voorop staan. Als familiebedrijf combineren zij vakmanschap met korte lijnen en een no-nonsense mentaliteit.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Ons bedrijf is onderdeel van de snelgroeiende&nbsp;<strong>VDK Groep</strong>, maar opereren met een eigen identiteit en cultuur. Je voelt je thuis bij&nbsp;<strong>Visser Elektrotechniek</strong>, terwijl je kunt bouwen op de kracht van de VDK Groep. Dit betekent; Extra voordelen zoals stabiliteit, volop opleidingskansen, doorgroeimogelijkheden en veel extra secundaire arbeidsvoorwaarden! De VDK Groep is medio April 2026 zo’n 180 bedrijven en ruim 7000 medewerkers groot en opererend in 6 Europese landen.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Contact</h3><p>Heb je interesse?</p><p>Bel, mail of app dan met Nadine Verhage</p><p>Recruitment Business Partner</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Telefoon: 06-44871851</p><p>Email: <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>#LI-NV1</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/vdk-groep-bv/inspecteur-elektrotechniek-scios-nen-3140-beverwijk-461096","tags":["Arbo","kwaliteit","inspectie & milieu"],"job_types":["Entry","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Beverwijk, Noord-Holland, Nederland","created_at":1795816287},{"slug":"senior-legal-counsel-product-ai-part-time-amsterdam-176740","company_name":"Foleon","title":"Senior Legal Counsel - Product & AI (Part-time)","description":"<p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Amsterdam (hybrid) | Part-time (freelance) 8 hours a week | €2,000 to €2,500 per month </strong></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#3f4149"><br></span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#3f4149">Foleon is a leading content creation platform providing business teams with a fast and scalable way to produce highly-engaging content experiences that bring a new level of intelligence to their customer journeys.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#3f4149">Foleon is based in Amsterdam and New York and serves more than 1,200 global B2B brands. We value people who are bold, ambitious, collaborative, and customer-centric. Even better, the ones who know how to work hard and have fun at the same time. We’re a team of highly driven people, with a great sense of human connection and a clear focus.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#3f4149">Your Mission</span></strong></p><p>As our Senior Product &amp; AI Counsel, you’ll own the legal side of our product and AI proposition, working with us about one day a week on a retainer basis. It’s a new role. You’ll work closely with Product, Engineering and leadership to make sure what we build and ship holds up under the EU AI Act, cybersecurity law, digital accessibility rules and GDPR.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#3f4149">Your Job</span></strong></p><ul><li><p>Act as our product counsel: join product syncs, review features before they’re built, and flag legal and compliance questions early.</p></li><li><p>Lead compliance for our AI proposition: classify our AI use cases, map our obligations as a provider or deployer under the EU AI Act, and set up the documentation, transparency and governance it requires.</p></li><li><p>Make sure our platform, and the content our customers publish with it, meets the European Accessibility Act and related standards.</p></li><li><p>Build privacy into the product by advising on GDPR questions tied to new features and data.</p></li><li><p>Advise on cybersecurity law, including NIS2, the Cyber Resilience Act and incident reporting duties, working closely with our security team.</p></li><li><p>Track changes in AI, cybersecurity, accessibility and privacy regulation, and turn them into practical guidance for the team.</p></li></ul> <br> <p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#3f4149">Your Competencies &amp; Skills</span></strong></p><ul class="ak-ul"><li><p>Senior and independent: you make calls and own them, without someone steering you.</p></li><li><p>A practical communicator who explains complex regulation to product teams in plain language, with answers instead of memos full of caveats.</p></li><li><p>Proactive and curious: you spot gaps before they become problems and want to understand how the product actually works.</p></li><li><p>Comfortable working part-time and flexibly, and available when something urgent comes up.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#3f4149">Your Qualifications</span></strong></p><ul><li><p>A Master’s in Law (or equivalent) and 6+ years of experience, ideally a mix of law firm and in-house at a tech or SaaS company.</p></li><li><p>Hands-on experience as product counsel for software, ideally including AI products.</p></li><li><p>Deep working knowledge of the EU AI Act and how it applies to AI propositions in practice.</p></li><li><p>Experience with cybersecurity law (NIS2, Cyber Resilience Act) and digital accessibility rules (European Accessibility Act).</p></li><li><p>A solid grounding in commercial and corporate law, with working knowledge of employment law.</p></li><li><p>GDPR and privacy expertise is a plus, ideally at DPO level or with a certification such as CIPP/E.</p></li><li><p>Experience working with scale-ups on a retainer or fractional basis is a plus.</p></li><li><p>Fluent English. Dutch is a plus.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#3f4149">Note:</span></strong><span style="color:#3f4149"> All our hiring is done in-house, so we’re not looking for agency support for this role. Thanks for understanding!</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/foleon/senior-legal-counsel-product-ai-part-time-amsterdam-176740","tags":[],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795816287},{"slug":"ai-engineer-rotterdam-303730","company_name":"Cefetra Group BV","title":"AI Engineer","description":"<p><strong><em>Do you thrive on complex problems and want to work at the forefront of AI? Join Cefetra Group’s new AI Innovation Hub as an AI Engineer and shape how AI creates value across our international trading business, from agents and workflows integrated with our core systems to the skills and ways of working that make them stick.</em></strong></p><p><strong>Who we are</strong></p><p>Cefetra Group comprises several trading companies in the agricultural sector and the food ingredients industry, with leading brands in the ingredients market. Together, we employ approximately 800 people across 39 offices in 17 countries worldwide. We work closely together to provide our customers with the best possible service. Together with our suppliers, we develop strong supply chains and create value by sourcing raw materials and supplying them to the international food, animal feed and energy industries. Behind that sits real complexity: global commodity flows, volatile markets, intricate contracts and logistics, and data spread across many entities and systems. That is exactly where AI can make a decisive difference, and we are building the capability to make it happen.</p><p><strong>The role</strong></p><p>As an AI Engineer in the AI Innovation Hub, part of the Group Digital &amp; Technology team, your goal is to build Cefetra Group’s AI capability and set the standard for how AI is designed and used across our entities. You’ll deliver AI solutions, from agents and workflows to knowledge bases, that teams across Cefetra Group can apply to augment their work, while helping colleagues build the skills to use them. You’ll work directly with process owners and business leaders to find where AI creates the most value. The AI Innovation Hub is just getting started, so together with the Group Digital &amp; Technology team you’ll shape its direction from the ground up: which opportunities it pursues and how it delivers them. You’ll also work with Builders and Changemakers, colleagues in our entities who build AI solutions and drive adoption, to share what works and show business leaders what AI makes possible.</p><p><strong>Your responsibilities include</strong></p><ul><li><p>Run discovery workshops to identify bottlenecks, value and exceptions. Assess use cases against readiness, team commitment, expected value and reuse potential.</p></li><li><p>Build AI workflows and agents using company data. Take prototypes all the way to robust, production-grade solutions that teams rely on in their daily work.</p></li><li><p>Integrate AI solutions with ERP, finance and operations systems, designing integrations that move safely from read-only access to controlled write-back.</p></li><li><p>Test solutions against real business scenarios. Set the deployment patterns, tool choices and safeguards that others across Cefetra Group build on.</p></li><li><p>Deliver hands-on workshops, from practical AI topics such as Claude Skills for non-technical colleagues to technical topics such as Model Context Protocol (MCP) for Builders and create materials Changemakers can use to train their peers.</p></li><li><p>Prepare demos of working use cases for leadership briefings.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Who you are</strong></p><p>To succeed at Cefetra Group, you love complexity and combine deep technical curiosity with a pragmatic, collaborative approach. You work well both independently and with people at all levels of Cefetra Group. You take ownership end to end and move easily between governance, technical details and business priorities. You also meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li><p>You have at least four years of experience in a technical, customer-facing, consulting or product role.</p></li><li><p>You’ve built and evaluated large language model (LLM) workflows, agents or applications in production.</p></li><li><p>You have hands-on experience with retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), embeddings, vector search, indexing, knowledge bases, context engineering and orchestration.</p></li><li><p>You follow AI developments closely, from new models to agentic patterns and protocols, and know how to turn new capabilities into practical value.</p></li><li><p>You have full-stack development experience with Python or TypeScript, including APIs, authentication, data transformation and enterprise integrations.</p></li><li><p>You’re fluent in English and have led workshops for non-technical audiences.</p></li></ul><p><strong>What we offer</strong></p><p>A unique opportunity to help Cefetra Group grow and become part of a dynamic and entrepreneurial team within an established multinational. We’re always open to discussing your individual needs. Here’s what we offer.</p><ul><li><p>Access to frontier AI models and the room to experiment with new tools, techniques and ways of working.</p></li><li><p>Flexible working hours and hybrid working, as well as opportunities to learn and develop.</p></li><li><p>An excellent remuneration and benefits package, including a competitive base salary, holiday allowance, an attractive bonus scheme and 28 days of annual leave.</p></li><li><p>An office in one of the finest locations in central Rotterdam, overlooking the Maas and the Erasmus Bridge, with plenty of social activities and excellent coffee.</p></li></ul><p><strong>If this sounds like you</strong></p><p>Interested in a conversation to further explore and enquire? Please apply below and we will contact you a.s.a.p. Or contact <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ----- Lemmers</a> via <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="tel:+31625203984">+31 6 2520 3984</a> or <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- He will be happy to tell you more about this opportunity and the recruitment process.</p><p><strong>Recruitment, consulting other temp/secondment agency?</strong></p><p>We appreciate the interest, but we seek all our candidates directly. We understand that you would like to present your candidates our interesting positions, but this is not how we have structured our recruitment process. This means that all unsolicited profiles offered will be treated as direct applications to our vacancies.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/cefetra-group-bv/ai-engineer-rotterdam-303730","tags":["Cefetra Group"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Rotterdam, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795816287},{"slug":"partner-manager-emea-north-netherlands-93425","company_name":"N8N","title":"Partner Manager EMEA North","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The AI orchestration of your wildest imagination.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">n8n is the open workflow orchestration platform built for the new era of AI. 