&lt;div class=&quot;has-nudge&quot; data-nudge-id=&quot;5eb9419b-6a4d-4451-bfa6-e2eb96084be0&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Various health plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off plans for vacation and sick time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental leave options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office perks, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;has-nudge&quot; data-nudge-id=&quot;5eb9419b-6a4d-4451-bfa6-e2eb96084be0&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Learn more about Zscaler&#39;s hybrid working model and benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zscaler.com/candidate-resource-hub&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By applying for this role, you adhere to applicable laws, regulations, and Zscaler policies, including those related to security and privacy standards and guidelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Zscaler is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all individuals. We strive to create a workplace where employees are treated with respect and have the chance to succeed. All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy or related medical conditions), age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws. &lt;em&gt;See more information by clicking on the &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12ScreenRdr.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;link.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pay Transparency&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zscaler complies with all applicable federal, state, and local pay transparency rules.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zscaler is committed to providing reasonable support (called accommodations or adjustments) in our recruiting processes for candidates who are differently abled, have long term conditions, mental health conditions or sincerely held religious beliefs, or who are neurodivergent or require pregnancy-related support.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/zscaler/staff-devops-engineer-ai-security-105468","tags":["AI Guard"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1795773323},{"slug":"senior-security-engineer-ai-application-security-amsterdam-482827","company_name":"Datasnipper","title":"Senior Security Engineer, AI & Application Security","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a seasoned Senior Security Engineer, focused on AI &amp; Application Security, to join our Platform team in Amsterdam. Working in a bootstrapped and profitable scaleup, you'll take a proactive, hands-on, senior role securing our agentic AI products, owning an emerging and fast-growing area of security engineering, the risks that come specifically from building with LLMs and autonomous agents, while helping raise the bar on our broader application security practices.<br /><br /><strong>Why DataSnipper?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>The hardest AI problems aren't about getting an answer fast. They're about getting one people can trust.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe trust is essential to how society works. Every day, we rely on information that's been independently verified, from financial statements to the products we buy, to the sustainability claims companies make. Behind that trust are audit and finance professionals who examine evidence, verify information and hold organizations accountable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At DataSnipper, we build AI solutions that empower those professionals. By making evidence easier to trace and verify, we help them focus on the judgment and expertise that make their work so important.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>For our product and engineering team, this is where things get exciting.</strong> In audit, a plausible answer isn't good enough. Every output has to be explainable and traceable back to its source. We've just launched a brand new agentic platform, Alwin by DataSnipper. AI agents running in the cloud across hundreds of documents at once, reasoning across PDF, Word and Excel, with a full audit trail behind every step. There are lots of greenfield problems ahead, and real room to shape what we build and how we build it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And we build at scale. More than <strong>600,000 professionals across 3,000+ organizations in 175 countries</strong> rely on DataSnipper, including Fortune 500 companies, government agencies and all Big Four audit firms. In 2025 alone, the DataSnipper platform delivered more than <strong>$1.4 billion in productivity savings to is customers</strong>. Backed by a $100 million Series B led by Index Ventures, at a $1 billion valuation, and as proud members of 1% for the Planet, we care about how we grow, not just how fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you want to build AI that professionals trust with work that really matters, <em>this is your chance to help shape the future of audit and finance and do the best work of your career along the way.</em></p><h2><br /><br />What You Will Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own AI-specific security as a discipline at DataSnipper: identify, assess, and mitigate the risks unique to LLM-based and agentic systems across our products and platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate security policies and risk requirements into concrete technical controls, standards, and guardrails, in partnership with Legal and technical teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a proactive AI security practice grounded in frameworks such as the OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications, the broader OWASP GenAI Security Project (including agentic security), MITRE ATLAS, and the NIST AI Risk Management Framework, and adapt them to how we build.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Threat model our agentic features and pipelines, covering prompt injection, sensitive information disclosure, data and model poisoning, insecure output handling, excessive agency, supply-chain risk, and unsafe tool and API use.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Red team our AI systems, probing models, prompts, agents, and integrations for weaknesses before attackers do, and turn findings into concrete fixes and guardrails.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and help implement guardrails, input/output validation, sandboxing, least-privilege tool access, and monitoring for AI and agent behavior.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embed security into how we build AI, shifting security left through secure-by-design guidance, secure SDLC practices, and design and code reviews for AI features.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with product and engineering teams to make secure AI the default, providing patterns, tooling, and guidance rather than after-the-fact gatekeeping.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strengthen our overall security engineering posture alongside the SRE team, contributing to our SOC 2 and compliance efforts (e.g. via Vanta), CI/CD security gates, and the principle that vulnerable code cannot get deployed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own our vulnerability management process: identify and prioritize vulnerabilities based on risk, drive remediation across engineering and platform teams, track findings to closure, and fix recurring findings at the root.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strengthen identity and access management, secrets management, and encryption across our products and platform, including the credentials and access that agents and AI integrations depend on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish detection, logging, and incident response practices for AI-specific threats, and help the team respond when they occur.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay ahead of a rapidly evolving threat landscape and continuously raise the bar for how we secure AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Promote secure development practices through developer guidance and trainings, awareness initiatives, and collaboration with engineering teams.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You Bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Minimum 5 years of experience in security engineering, application security, or a closely related field, with a track record of owning security work end to end in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong grounding in application and cloud security fundamentals: threat modeling, secure design, common vulnerability classes, and secure SDLC practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with SAST, DAST, SCA, API Security, Threat Modeling and Vulnerability Management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with identity and access management, secrets management, and encryption implementations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated interest and hands-on experience in AI/LLM security, whether through professional work, research, red teaming, CTFs, or personal projects, and familiarity with frameworks like the OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications or MITRE ATLAS.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of how LLM-based and agentic systems work in practice, including prompts, tool/function calling, retrieval, and agent orchestration, and where they break.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in a scripting or programming language (Python preferred) to build tooling, automate checks, and prototype mitigations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience securing cloud-native systems, ideally on Azure, including CI/CD pipelines (e.g. GitHub) and infrastructure-as-code.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proactive, builder mindset; you prevent problems by shipping guardrails and enabling teams, not just by finding issues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication skills; able to explain AI-specific risks and tradeoffs to engineers, product managers, and leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Entrepreneurial mindset with the ability to thrive in a fast-moving scale-up, set technical direction, influence without authority, and mentor other engineers while defining a practice that doesn't yet have a playbook.</p></li></ul><h2>Preferred Qualifications</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience red teaming or pentesting AI/LLM systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with the OWASP GenAI Security Project's agentic security work and emerging standards for securing autonomous agents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with AI security tooling such as guardrail frameworks, LLM firewalls, prompt-injection scanners, or AI red-teaming tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience implementing security controls in production agentic systems, including sandboxing, least-privilege tool access, and runtime monitoring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with compliance frameworks (SOC 2, ISO 27001) and tools like Vanta.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with observability and monitoring tooling (e.g. Grafana).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relevant security certifications (e.g. OSCP, GIAC, or AI-security-specific credentials).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in fintech, audit technology, or other regulated, trust-sensitive domains.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with responsible AI, model governance, or AI safety concepts.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be part of one of the fastest-growing, profitable unicorn scale-ups in the Netherlands with a global impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity (Stock Appreciation Rights) to share the company's success and growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension plan with a 6% contribution on top of your base salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">28 vacation days per year (full-time) to support your work-life balance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid work model with at least 3 days onsite in our dynamic Amsterdam office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Daily, freshly prepared lunches by our in-house chef to keep you energized</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">NS business card for easy commuting to the office if applicable</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to continuous learning and development initiatives to grow your skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engage with a vibrant international team spread across five global offices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company-wide events like DataSnipper GO, where global teams come together</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to a mental health and wellness platform supporting your wellbeing</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Recruitment Process</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruitment Screen (30 minutes, online)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hiring Manager Interview (30 minutes, online)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assessment Interview (60 minutes, on-site)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final Interview (30 minutes, online)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>At DataSnipper, we believe great ideas come from different perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds. We are committed to building an inclusive workplace and providing every candidate with a fair and equitable hiring experience.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Our hiring decisions are merit-based and grounded in the skills, experience, potential, and capabilities relevant to the role.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We welcome applicants regardless of age, race, ethnicity, nationality, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, disability, or any other characteristic that makes you, you.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>What matters to us is what you can bring to the role, the team, and DataSnipper.</em> 🚀</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/datasnipper/senior-security-engineer-ai-application-security-amsterdam-482827","tags":["Finance & Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795772425},{"slug":"frontend-engineer-eindhoven-355284","company_name":"Aim Solutions","title":"Frontend Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Eindhoven, the Netherlands (on-site, High Tech Campus) | <strong>Type:</strong> Full-time | <strong>Level:</strong> Medior–Senior, ~3–5 years of relevant experience</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AIM Solutions is an early-stage deep-tech startup in Eindhoven building inspection and metrology equipment for the semiconductor industry. We are in an active build phase: a small, growing team turning lab setups into a tool that does not exist anywhere else yet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Frontend Engineer you own the web applications people use to run our instrument and read its results: an operator console that configures and runs scans with live camera and stage data, and a reconstruction front-end for setting up runs and inspecting images. Your users are the engineers in our lab, so feedback is immediate. You work closely with the Embedded, Software and Algorithm engineers who build the systems behind your interfaces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain the frontends of our acquisition and reconstruction applications, from design to release.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop real-time views of camera images, stage positions and scan progress streamed from the instrument.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design clear, safe operator workflows for configuring and running measurements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep a shared design system and component library across our applications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extend the Python and C# backends where a feature needs it, together with the backend owners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take part in code review and bring good frontend practice to the team: typing, testing, CI.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your profile</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">BSc or MSc in Computer Science, Software Engineering or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">~3–5 years of experience building production web applications with React and TypeScript.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with real-time or data-heavy interfaces (WebSockets, streaming data, canvas or WebGL rendering).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong CSS and a feel for clean, usable interface design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of Python or C# and REST APIs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Git and collaborative code review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full professional proficiency in English.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value judgment and ownership over a perfect match. If you recognize yourself in most of this, we would like to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building software for scientific instruments, industrial machines or other hardware.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with image or scientific data visualization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with FastAPI or ASP.NET Core, end-to-end testing (Playwright, Cypress), or working in a Scrum team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interest in optics, imaging or semiconductor metrology.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership of the user-facing software of a tool that does not exist anywhere else yet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A small team with short feedback loops and real impact on the product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work at the meeting point of software, optics and hardware, on the High Tech Campus Eindhoven.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A competitive salary for the Dutch market.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/aim-solutions/frontend-engineer-eindhoven-355284","tags":["Development & Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Headquarter","created_at":1795772425},{"slug":"senior-revenue-operations-manager-amsterdam-20459","company_name":"Perk","title":"Senior Revenue Operations Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong><br /><br />Perk (formerly TravelPerk) is the intelligent platform for travel and spend management. Built to tackle the time-consuming, manual work that gets in the way of real work, our tools automate everything from travel bookings to expenses, invoice processing, and more. By eliminating this shadow work that wastes hours, erodes morale, and saps innovation, we're on a mission to power real work, with real impact.<br /><br />We're trusted by more than 12,000 companies worldwide, including Bolt, GoCardless, and Fabletics, and we're tackling the 7 hours of lost productivity per employee each week, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.perk.com/shadow-work-report">a $1.7 trillion problem</a>.<br /><br />Founded in 2015, Perk has grown into a global company of more than 1,800 people across 12 offices globally, with headquarters in London and Boston. We combine innovation, control, and simplicity to transform how businesses work and how people feel at work.<br /><br />At Perk, we're driven by our values, like being an owner, delivering a 7-star experience, and working as one team. We value curiosity, purpose, and mindset, not just knowledge, to unlock the power in your potential. Our talent team brings together leading minds from the travel, fintech, and SaaS industries, representing over 70 countries. If you're excited about having a real impact and shaping how millions of people experience work, we'd love you on the team.<br /><br />Visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.perk.com">www.perk.com</a> to learn more.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div><div style="left:0px;width:100%;height:0px;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%"><iframe src="https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/4899a966-8724-4480-958f-7271e5dc2807/f3e1915d-e346-4987-a1fb-9c447e8786c0" style="top:0px;left:0px;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0px" allowfullscreen="true" scrolling="no" allow="encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation"></iframe></div></div><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a <strong>Senior Revenue Operations Manager</strong> to join our Revenue Operations team and act as a broad, senior partner to our revenue organisation. You'll run the complex analysis and modelling behind target setting and annual planning for the entire commercial organisation. You will also help the Director set and execute the revenue analytics strategy, and run the insights that shape how revenue leadership sees the business. As you ramp up, you will take on growing ownership of the forecasting cadence alongside the Director of Revenue Operations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for someone with very strong analytical and modelling skills, which are the foundation of the role, especially in your first two quarters. Just as important, we want someone who is commercially minded and keen to grow into a generalist role, broadening from there into revenue insights and forecasting.</p><h2><br /><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">First 90 days: Scope the revenue analytics strategy and build the core dashboards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">First 180 days: Lead the analysis for the annual planning and target-setting cycle, and automate the core of revenue reporting and insights with AI tooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">First 12 months: Take on co-ownership of the forecasting cadence with the Director of Revenue Operations.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What Will You Be Doing?</strong></h2><h3>Run Complex Modelling &amp; Analysis</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run complex analysis and modelling to support target setting and the annual planning process for the entire commercial organisation, made up of around 600 commercial roles across SDRs, AEs and Account Managers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain the models behind target setting: capacity, quota and productivity assumptions, and territory and segment allocation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Frame the key planning questions, choose the method, pressure-test scenarios and sensitivities, and deliver clear recommendations to revenue leadership, explaining the trade-offs in plain language.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work as the senior analytical partner to the other analyst on the team: stay hands-on in the models while setting the quality bar and documentation standards, so each planning cycle is repeatable and auditable.</p></li></ul><h3>Build the Revenue Analytics Strategy</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the Director of Revenue Operations to define the revenue analytics strategy: what we need to build across Salesforce and Looker, and in what order.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Map the current reporting landscape — what exists, what's trusted, what's duplicated or out of date — and use that map to shape the build plan.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own execution of that plan: build and maintain the core dashboards and reports that revenue leadership and the wider commercial organisation rely on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Launch and run a recurring insights digest for revenue leaders, turning dashboards and data into a clear narrative — what changed, why it matters, what to do about it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring a point of view on what's worth building versus what's noise, and be willing to push back on requests that don't earn their keep.</p></li></ul><h3>Grow Into Forecasting</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Co-run the forecasting cadence with sales leaders and the Director of Revenue Operations — forecast calls, pipeline reviews, and accuracy tracking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and refine forecasting models based on pipeline, productivity, and historical conversion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct strategic analyses to determine forecasting trends and identify opportunities for process improvement.</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>What You’ll Bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience in Revenue or Sales Operations, preferably in a SaaS or technology company operating at a global or European level.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced modelling and scenario analysis skills (spreadsheets and SQL), ideally with experience in target setting, capacity planning or annual planning for a large commercial organisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid Salesforce reporting skills and working fluency in a BI tool (Looker or equivalent), with a practical, business-first approach to data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial judgement and exposure to quota-carrying teams such as Account Executives, plus a generalist mindset: as comfortable building a dashboard as a planning model or running a forecasting call.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to influence sales leadership and revenue executives, and to own ambiguous problems end to end, from framing the question to landing the recommendation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written communication, since the insights digest is a core, ongoing deliverable of this role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience using AI tools to automate analysis and reporting, or a clear appetite to build that skill quickly.</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>What We Offer </strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days of annual leave to rest and recharge, plus all public holidays.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An optional pension scheme to support your long-term financial wellbeing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A tax-efficient bike leasing scheme through Lease a Bike, for your commute or personal use.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reimbursed commuting costs if you live more than 10km away from the office.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation paired with equity in Perk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unforgettable team experiences, including our annual summer party.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive wellbeing support through Spring Health, offering fast access to 12 therapy and 12 coaching sessions for you and your loved ones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Focus on your family with 12-16 weeks’ paid parental leave</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">16 paid volunteer hours each year to give back to causes you care about.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Up to 20 “Work From Anywhere” days annually to explore the world while staying connected.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A fully paid four-week sabbatical after five years with Perk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relocation support to help you move seamlessly into one of our hubs.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at Perk</strong><br />AI is embedded in how we work across every function. The tools you'll use day-to-day are AI-enabled so you can move faster and spend more time on the work that matters. In practice, that means using AI to research and prioritise accounts, draft and refine outreach, handle customer interactions more effectively, synthesise information, and cut through shadow work - the invisible tasks that pull people away from the work only they can do - so you can focus on relationships and outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How We Work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Perk, we take an IRL-first approach to work, where our team works together in-person 3 days a week. As such, this role requires you to be based within commuting distance of our hubs. We fundamentally believe in the value of meeting in real life to improve connectivity, productivity, creativity and ultimately making us a great place to work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For certain roles, we can help with relocation from anywhere in the world, English is the official language at the office. Please submit your resume in English if you choose to apply. Do not forget to submit an updated portfolio and/or resume.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perk is a global company with a diverse customer base, and we want to make sure the people behind our product reflect that. We’re an equal opportunity employer, which means you’re welcome at Perk regardless of how you look, where you’re from, or anything else that makes you, well, you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Protect Yourself from Recruitment Scams</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">All official communication from Perk will always come from email addresses ending in @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://perk.com">perk.com</a> or @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://externalperk.com">externalperk.com</a>, our verified social media channels, or recruiters listed on our official LinkedIn page. We will never ask you to pay for equipment, training, or fees, request sensitive personal information such as bank details early in the process, or communicate through unofficial apps like WhatsApp, Telegram, or Signal. If you receive a message claiming to be from Perk that seems suspicious, please do not respond. Forward it to <u>security [at] perk .com</u>, and we will confirm whether it is legitimate.<br /><br />#LI-Hybrid</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/perk/senior-revenue-operations-manager-amsterdam-20459","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795772419},{"slug":"commissions-targets-manager-amsterdam-78492","company_name":"Perk","title":"Commissions & Targets Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong><br /><br />Perk (formerly TravelPerk) is the intelligent platform for travel and spend management. Built to tackle the time-consuming, manual work that gets in the way of real work, our tools automate everything from travel bookings to expenses, invoice processing, and more. By eliminating this shadow work that wastes hours, erodes morale, and saps innovation, we're on a mission to power real work, with real impact.<br /><br />We're trusted by more than 12,000 companies worldwide, including Bolt, GoCardless, and Fabletics, and we're tackling the 7 hours of lost productivity per employee each week, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.perk.com/shadow-work-report">a $1.7 trillion problem</a>.<br /><br />Founded in 2015, Perk has grown into a global company of more than 1,800 people across 12 offices globally, with headquarters in London and Boston. We combine innovation, control, and simplicity to transform how businesses work and how people feel at work.<br /><br />At Perk, we're driven by our values, like being an owner, delivering a 7-star experience, and working as one team. We value curiosity, purpose, and mindset, not just knowledge, to unlock the power in your potential. Our talent team brings together leading minds from the travel, fintech, and SaaS industries, representing over 70 countries. If you're excited about having a real impact and shaping how millions of people experience work, we'd love you on the team.<br /><br />Visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.perk.com">www.perk.com</a> to learn more.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div><div style="left:0px;width:100%;height:0px;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%"><iframe src="https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/4899a966-8724-4480-958f-7271e5dc2807/f3e1915d-e346-4987-a1fb-9c447e8786c0" style="top:0px;left:0px;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0px" allowfullscreen="true" scrolling="no" allow="encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation"></iframe></div></div><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a Commissions &amp; Targets Manager to own how our sales organisation is paid and how its targets are set. You'll run the commission process end to end, manage CaptivateIQ, handle complex cases, and run the quarterly target distribution for our sales reps. You'll shape our commission strategy with the Director of Revenue Operations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll also be the go-to person for two experienced commission analysts. It's not a line management role, but you'll guide the team on difficult cases. Payouts depend on accurate numbers delivered on fixed deadlines, so we need someone with strong attention to detail who prioritises well in a fast-moving team.<br /><br />This is an Individual Contributor role.</p><h2><br /><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First 90 days:</strong> Master our commission plans, workflows, and CaptivateIQ setup, and execute your first end-of-quarter close with support from the Director.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First 6 months:</strong> Take full ownership of the end-of-quarter close and case escalations, and lead your first quarterly target distribution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First 12 months:</strong> Partner with the Director to shape our commission strategy while optimising the processes and system configurations you inherited.</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>What Will You Be Doing?</strong></h2><h3><strong>Commission Processes</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the end-of-quarter commission process, from data validation and plan calculations to review, approvals and payout handover. Start with the Director's oversight and take full ownership of the process within your first two quarters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define the end-of-quarter schedule: map all the activities, decide which to prioritise, identify what can be front-loaded ahead of quarter end, and build a plan that hits the deadlines and delivers quality results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">During the close, make quick calls and reprioritise when things go wrong, flag risks before they affect payouts, and keep the process documented and auditable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spot recurring errors and bottlenecks, and fix them at the source.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Commission Cases &amp; Team Support</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the escalation point for complex or disputed commission cases, supporting the two commission analysts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coach the analysts on case handling, resolve difficult cases and make clear, consistent and well-documented decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify patterns in the cases raised, and use them to improve plan rules, documentation and communication.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Commission System Ownership</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage our commissions system, CaptivateIQ: plan configuration, data integrations, quarterly updates and access.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the Sales Operations, Finance and Data team on data quality and any system changes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Test and validate changes before each close, so that calculations are accurate and reproducible.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Commission Strategy</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with the Director of Revenue Operations to define the commission strategy, including plan design, rules and how they support company goals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analyse plan performance and its effect on sales behaviour, and bring a point of view on what to change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare the commission plan updates for each planning period and communicate them clearly to sales and finance stakeholders.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Quarterly Target Distribution</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the target setting cycle each quarter, with clear methodology and timelines, and explain the outcomes to sales leaders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make sure any outlier or special case target adjustments are handled before the targets are published.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Handle target questions and adjustments in a fair and consistent way.</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>What Will You Need to Succeed?</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience in Sales Operations, Revenue Operations, Sales Compensation or a similar role, preferably in a SaaS or technology company operating at a global or European level.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience running commission processes for a quota-carrying sales organisation, including end-of-quarter closes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience administering a commissions system (CaptivateIQ or a similar tool such as Qobra) is preferred but not required.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional attention to detail and the discipline to deliver accurate results on fixed deadlines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong ability to improve processes: you spot what is manual, error-prone or slow, and fix it at the source.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to prioritise well and make fast, accurate calls in a fast-moving, deadline-driven environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical skills. Experience setting or contributing to sales targets and quotas is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good judgment and strong stakeholder management, including handling sensitive conversations about pay with sales leaders, finance and ICs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience guiding or coaching other analysts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear written and verbal communication in English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with global or multi-region teams is a plus.<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We Offer?</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days of annual leave to rest and recharge, plus all public holidays.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An optional pension scheme to support your long-term financial wellbeing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A tax-efficient bike leasing scheme through Lease a Bike, for your commute or personal use.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reimbursed commuting costs if you live more than 10km away from the office.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation paired with equity in Perk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unforgettable team experiences, including our annual summer party.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive wellbeing support through Spring Health, offering fast access to 12 therapy and 12 coaching sessions for you and your loved ones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Focus on your family with 12-16 weeks’ paid parental leave</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">16 paid volunteer hours each year to give back to causes you care about.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Up to 20 “Work From Anywhere” days annually to explore the world while staying connected.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A fully paid four-week sabbatical after five years with Perk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relocation support to help you move seamlessly into one of our hubs.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at Perk</strong><br />AI is embedded in how we work across every function. The tools you'll use day-to-day are AI-enabled so you can move faster and spend more time on the work that matters. In practice, that means using AI to research and prioritise accounts, draft and refine outreach, handle customer interactions more effectively, synthesise information, and cut through shadow work - the invisible tasks that pull people away from the work only they can do - so you can focus on relationships and outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How We Work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Perk, we take an IRL-first approach to work, where our team works together in-person 3 days a week. As such, this role requires you to be based within commuting distance of our hubs. We fundamentally believe in the value of meeting in real life to improve connectivity, productivity, creativity and ultimately making us a great place to work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For certain roles, we can help with relocation from anywhere in the world, English is the official language at the office. Please submit your resume in English if you choose to apply. Do not forget to submit an updated portfolio and/or resume.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perk is a global company with a diverse customer base, and we want to make sure the people behind our product reflect that. We’re an equal opportunity employer, which means you’re welcome at Perk regardless of how you look, where you’re from, or anything else that makes you, well, you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Protect Yourself from Recruitment Scams</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">All official communication from Perk will always come from email addresses ending in @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://perk.com">perk.com</a> or @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://externalperk.com">externalperk.com</a>, our verified social media channels, or recruiters listed on our official LinkedIn page. We will never ask you to pay for equipment, training, or fees, request sensitive personal information such as bank details early in the process, or communicate through unofficial apps like WhatsApp, Telegram, or Signal. If you receive a message claiming to be from Perk that seems suspicious, please do not respond. Forward it to <u>security [at] perk .com</u>, and we will confirm whether it is legitimate.<br /><br />#LI-Hybrid</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/perk/commissions-targets-manager-amsterdam-78492","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795772419},{"slug":"software-engineer-java-security-amsterdam-78497","company_name":"Teampicnic","title":"Software Engineer (Java) - Security","description":"&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-intro-section&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section-inner&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;entry-intro&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In a nutshell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Picnic, we&#39;re building the most secure milkman on earth. Our Security team owns the security tooling that protects Picnic, and we&#39;re looking for a Java Engineer to make it work everywhere: connecting our systems to those tools, automating checks across the whole company, and strengthening how we manage identity and access.&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll be the engineer in the Security team. Instead of writing policies, you&#39;ll write the code that wires our security systems into the rest of Picnic, and you&#39;ll help product teams do the right thing by default.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tricks of the trade&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Take ownership of projects from concept to delivery, aligning technical solutions with business goals with a product engineering mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform work:&lt;/strong&gt; Own Picnic’s core Security and IAM platform services, and build integrations with internal and external services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identity &amp;amp; Access:&lt;/strong&gt; Help take our IAM initiative from MVP to production. Look at the options, build or integrate the pieces and connect them to the systems Picnic runs on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Work closely with development teams to integrate security best practices into the software development lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Ambassador: &lt;/strong&gt;Conduct application security workshops to raise awareness and promote secure coding practices among developers.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Tech:&lt;/strong&gt; Java 21/25 (Spring 6 with Spring Boot 3.5, Reactor, Immutables, Maven), React, Angular, RabbitMQ, Kafka, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Git, Docker, AWS, Helm, Terraform, Kubernetes, Vault, Datadog, Python 3.x&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a Master’s Degree (in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Information Technology, Computer Engineering or a related technical field) or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have at least 3-7 years of professional experience with Java.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine curiosity about security: experience isn’t required, but you’re excited to dive into topics like access control and to grow into the domain with us.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your English skills are on point (no Dutch required).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re based in or happy to relocate to the Netherlands*&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For bonus points:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Security frameworks like NIST, CIS Controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working experience in IAM integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work from our office in Amsterdam. Being present makes a genuine difference to your team and the work. There&#39;s flexibility to work from home when needed, but if remote or hybrid-first is what you&#39;re after, this probably isn&#39;t the right fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Picnic Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;✍🏼 Every expert was once a beginner!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get plenty of opportunities to challenge yourself and grow, including the Picnic Tech Academy, Lunch &amp;amp; Learn sessions, and tailored soft skills training. We also offer free professional weekly language courses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💡 Make a difference&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work in an awesome startup environment with the freedom to drive your own projects and create a visible impact. Our fully electric vehicles and sustainable business model mean you’ll also be contributing to making the world a better place!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🫱🏼‍🫲🏾 Teamwork makes the dream work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With more than 80 nationalities across 3 countries, you’ll be part of a diverse company with plenty of cool stuff to get involved with, from board game evenings to after-work drinks to our company ski trip and more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🍎 You are what you eat&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get freshly prepared, healthy lunches and snacks (with plenty of vegetarian, vegan, and halal options). Coffee snob? Don’t worry, our amazing Picnic barista has you covered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🚴🏽 Stay healthy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mental health is important. As well as having the option to speak with Picnic colleagues who act as confidential advisors, our collaboration with OpenUp gives you easy access to professional psychologists, along with workshops and materials. There are plenty of sports communities and events to get involved with, from tennis to yoga, to climbing!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🔋 Attractive package&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer competitive compensation and a pension plan that looks out for your future self, as well as 25 vacation days per year, so you can recharge your batteries&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌍 Benefits for expats&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It can be daunting starting a new job AND moving to a new country. That’s why we offer lots of support for our many expat colleagues, if you want to find our relocation benefits, see &lt;a href=&quot;https://jobs.picnic.app/en/relocation&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/teampicnic/software-engineer-java-security-amsterdam-78497","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795762532},{"slug":"senior-project-manager-microsoft-dynamics-365-veenendaal-183507","company_name":"Hsogroupbv","title":"Senior Project Manager Microsoft Dynamics 365","description":"&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complexe projecten, volop mogelijkheden om te groeien en werken bij één van de top Microsoft system integrators van Nederland. Als Senior Project manager ben je verantwoordelijk voor de implementatie van Microsoft technologie en geef je leiding aan het projectteam van HSO.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We bouwen steeds vaker oplossingen voor klanten die niet alleen ERP willen, maar die bewust kiezen voor het Microsoft Cloud platform. En dus bijvoorbeeld ook kiezen voor Dynamics 365 for CRM, Field Service en Power BI. Omdat HSO één van de weinige Microsoft system integrators is, kunnen we klanten deze totaaloplossing bieden. De complexe en grotere internationale projecten vragen veel expertise en ervaring, Dus we hebben volop werk en uitdaging!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ben jij gewend om grootschalige Microsoft applicatie projecten te leiden?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wat ga je doen?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Als Senior Project manager schakel je continu tussen de belangen van de klant en HSO. De projecten zijn bovengemiddeld complex van aard en de stakeholders zijn vaak over meerdere bedrijven en de wereld verspreid. Dit is geen uitdaging maar gesneden koek voor jou.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jij beschikt over:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ten minste 5 jaar ervaring met ERP-implementaties als Project manager;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Je deelt onze mind set: je bent een kritische denker, een ondernemende zelf starter en je verbindt je met het resultaat;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Je business English is dik in orde, gezien onze internationale projecten;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Je management vaardigheden zijn consulterend, anticiperend en voorstellend van aard en gebruikt deze eigenschappen om mensen met je mee te krijgen en effectief te laten functioneren;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ervaring met het Microsoft-platform, Dynamics AX 2012 of Dynamics 365 is een pre;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aantoonbare kennis van methodieken voor project management zowel waterval als Agile, bijvoorbeeld PRINCE II, PMI- of IPMA C/D-certificering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wat bieden we jou?   &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Werken bij HSO is uitdagend, we willen je daar graag een goede beloning voor teruggeven. Naast goede primaire voordelen bieden wij: &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Een competitief salaris en een jaarlijkse bonus op basis van bedrijfs-, team- en individuele prestaties&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mobiliteitsvergoeding waarbij je of een auto kunt leasen of het bedrag toe kunt voegen aan je salaris. Daarbovenop krijg 100% betaald van de ov-kosten;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 vakantiedagen met de mogelijkheid om er 35 van te maken; &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybride werken, vanuit huis, op kantoor (Rotterdam, Veenendaal) of zelfs tijdens je Workation; &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EUR 65,- netto vitaliteitsbudget – we vinden het belangrijk dat we gezond blijven en een veilige werkplek hebben, zowel op kantoor als remote; &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Je kunt deelnemen aan het leasefietsplan; &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;En vooral een leven lang leren. Op dag één start jouw onboardingprogramma, daarnaast krijg je een persoonlijk studiebudget dat je kunt inzetten voor jouw professionele ontwikkeling en ontvang je ook een GoodHabitz account, een online trainingstool voor je persoonlijke ontwikkeling.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vrijheid, flexibiliteit en fun &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Je werkt in een internationale omgeving met professionals met verschillende nationaliteiten. Een flexibele werkweek van 40, 36 of 32 uur behoort tot de mogelijkheden omdat wij van mening zijn dat jouw manier van werken bij jouw levensstijl moet passen. HSO heeft professionals in dienst die plezier hebben in hun werk en klaar staan voor elkaar. Om het plezier in ons werk nog groter te maken, organiseren we uiteraard teamuitjes en bedrijfsfeesten, maar ook wekelijkse zomerborrels op ons dakterras, allerlei sportactiviteiten en is er de mogelijkheid bij te dragen aan onze Maatschappelijk Verantwoord Ondernemen-werkzaamheden.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Over HSO  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HSO is de eerste full-service Microsoft Partner in Nederland. Samen met ruim 2500 getalenteerde medewerkers in Europa, Azië en Noord-Amerika verlenen we ondersteuning op lokaal en internationaal niveau aan industriële bedrijven, retailers, financiële en zakelijke dienstverleners en overheidsinstellingen. &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HSO is voortdurend op zoek naar nieuw talent. We blijven onze wereldwijde community uitbreiden en scheppen er plezier in om samen te werken met prestatiegerichte mensen met een ondernemersgeest. Professionals die voortdurend willen leren en innoveren. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solliciteren &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enthousiast? Heb je vragen vooraf? &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Neem dan contact op met Sander van den Bogaard op : -----
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
